3 STAE Community of Madrid
3 CTRY Spain
1 OCCU Señor de Gibraleón, Huelva y Deza
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} don '''Juan Alfonso de la Cerda'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Señor de Gibraleón
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VIZCAYA.htm#InigoLopezdied1077 FMG MedLands Vizcaya]
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CASTILE.htm#JuanAlfonsoCerdadied1347
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         JUAN Alfonso de la Cerda (in France [1295]-7 Aug 1347).  He lived most of his life in Portugal.  Señor de Gibraleón, Huelva, Real de Manzanares y Deza.  "Juan de la Cerda, hijo de Alonso de la Cerda" confirmed the privi
2 CONC leges of Gibraleón by charter dated 15 Feb 1320[1449].  "Luis de la Cerda y Juan de la Cerda su hermano" agreed a division of property by charter dated 15 Nov 1327[1450].  He finally left Portugal in 1337 to serve Alfonso XI King 
2 CONC of Castile.  He fought at the battle of Salado near Tarifa 30 Oct 1340, which marked the end of the Muslim invasions.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ([1310]) dona MARIA Afonso de Portugal, illegitimate daughter of DINIZ King of Portugal & his mistress Marina Gómez (-before 1340).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (Gibraleón 24 May 1340) as her second husband, MARÍA Fernández de Luna, widow of JUAN Alfonso de Haro Señor de Cameros, daughter of ARTAL de Luna [Ricohombre de Aragón] & his wife Constanza de Aragón Señora de Seg
2 CONC orbe (-[1347]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juan & his first wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         BEATRIZ de la Cerda (in Portugal [1311]-early 1325).  Betrothed to Infante don PEDRO de Aragón, Conde de Ribagorza y Ampurias, son of JAIME II King of Aragon & his second wife Blanche of Sicily (1305-Pisa 4 Nov 1381). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         ALPHONSE de la Cerda (in Portugal [1313]-in battle Quimperlé 1342).  He fought with his cousin Louis de la Cerda in the war of succession in Brittany. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    Juan had [two] illegitimate children by an unknown mistress or mistresses: 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT Martim Fernandes de Lacerda, era filho de D. Afonso Fernandes de Lacerda, Senhor de de Almendra e de sua mulher D. Luiza de Menezes.
2 CONT
2 CONT D. Afonso Fernandes de Lacerda era filho de D. João Affonso de Lacerda, Duque de Angoulême, Condeslavel de França, Senhor de Gibralion e de Guelva, que morreu em 1357 e de sua mulher D. Maria de Portugal, filha natural do Rei D. D
2 CONC ini z de Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT O Duque de Angoulême, era filho de D. Mathilde de Norbone e de D. Afonso de Lacerda, bem conhecido na historia por ter sido aclamado Rei de Castela, trono que pela força lhe tirou seu irmão o Rei Sancho IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT D. A!fonso de Lacerda era filho de D. Fernando de Lacerda e de sua mulher a Infanta D. Branca, filha de São Luiz, Rei de França.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hemerotecadigital.cm-lisboa.pt/Periodicos/ElucidarioNobiliarchico/V2/N10/N10_master/ElucidarioNobiliarchico_Vol2_N10_Out1929.pdf
