2 CONC ericus, domina Violanta et dominus Petrus" as the children of "Petro regi Aragonum" and his wife[562].  The Crónica de San Juan de la Peña records that Jaime II King of Aragon arranged the marriage of "su hermana Doña Violant" and
2 CONC  "Rubert fillo del rey Carlos"[563].  m (Rome Mar 1297) as his first wife, ROBERT of Sicily, son of CHARLES II King of Naples & Sicily [Anjou-Capet] & his wife Maria of Hungary (Royal Palace of the Torre de San Erasmo, near Capua 
2 CONC 1278-Château-Neuf, Naples 16/20 Jan 1343/4, bur Naples Santa Chiara).  Named in 1297 as heir to Sicily by Pope Boniface VIII.  Appointed perpetual Vicar-General in the island of Sicily by his father 24 Jun 1299.  Principe di Saler
