2 CONT Wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_III_of_Aragon
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter III of Aragon
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter's fleet landing at Trapani. Notice the king wearing the crown and directing the landing
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter the Great (Catalan: Pere el Gran, Spanish: Pedro el Grande; 1239, Valencia – 2 November 1285) was the King of Aragon (as Peter III) of Valencia and of Majorca (as Peter I), and Count of Barcelona (as Peter II) from 1276 to h
2 CONC is death. He conquered Sicily and became its king in 1282. He was one of the greatest of medieval Aragonese monarchs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [show]
2 CONT
