1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''FERNANDO de Aragón'''
2 CONT s/o PEDRO de Aragón (-after 1314) & CONSTANZA Mendez Pelita de Silva
2 CONT x?MARÍA Núñez, d/o NUÑO Fernández Cogominho & Margarita de Albarnaz.  
2 CONT
2 CONT PEDRO de Aragón (-after 1314).  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Pedro de Aragon" as the son of "el Rey D. Pedro" and "D. Ines Zapata"[579].  Bofarull names “Da Inés Zapata” as mother of the king’s illegitimate 
2 CONC children “D. Fernando señor de Albarracín, D. Pedro que casó en Portugal con Da Constanza Mendez Pelita, y D. Sancho castellan de Amposta : la hija…Da Teresa y casó con D. Garcia Romeu que murió sin sucesion” (no sources cited)[58
2 CONC 0].  Salazar y Castro records the testament of Isabel Queen of Portugal, dated 1314, in which she bequeathed money to “Don Pedro, mi hermano, y à su hijo, qualquiera de ellos, que quedàre por mi muerte”[581].  m (Portugal) CONSTAN
2 CONC ZA Mendez Pelita de Silva, daughter of SUERO Mendez de Silva & his wife María Annes Brochardo.  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos records that "D. Pedro de Aragon", son of "el Rey D. Pedro" and "D. Ines Zapata", married "D
2 CONC . Constança Mendez Petite"[582].  Pedro & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         PEDRO de Aragón
2 CONT b)         '''FERNANDO de Aragón .  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Pedro de Aragon, D. Fernando que fue asaz bueno, i casó" as the sons of "D. Pedro de Aragon" and his wife "D. Constança Mendez Petite"[584].  
2 CONC m MARÍA Núñez, daughter of NUÑO Fernández Cogominho & his wife Margarita de Albarnaz.  Salazar y Acha does not record Fernando’s marriage, although he says that he died “sin hijos”[585].  The primary source which confirms the info
2 CONC rmation has not been identified.''' 
2 CONT c)          CONSTANZA de Aragón 
2 CONT d)         TERESA Alfonso de Aragón
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ARAGON%20&%20CATALONIA.htm
2 CONT ----
