1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Philip of Artois
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip of Artois [1](1269 – September 11, 1298) was the son of Robert II of Artois, Count of Artois and Amicie de Courtenay. He was the Lord of Conches, Nonancourt, and Domfront.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Blanche de Dreux, daughter of John II, Duke of Brittany, and had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite (1285–1311), married in 1301 Louis, Count of Évreux
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert III of Artois (1287–1342)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (1288–1344), a nun at Poissy
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne (1289 – aft. 1347), married in 1301 in Senlis Gaston I, Count of Foix
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (1291 – January 22, 1365, Wijnendaele), Lady of Merode, married in 1309 in Paris John I, Marquis of Namur
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (1296–1368, Normandy), married John II of Ponthieu, Count of Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT He served under his father at the Battle of Furnes, where he was wounded. He never recovered, and died of the effects over a year later. His premature death led to a legal battle later, when Artois was left to his sister Mahaut ra
2 CONC ther than his son Robert.
