2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Eleanor of Guzman (ca 1310 – 1351) was a mistress of King Alfonso XI of Castile. She is known in Spanish as Leonor Núñez de Guzmán.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Seville, daughter of the Castilian nobles Pedro Núñez de Guzmán (descendant of the noble family of Saint Dominic) and Juana Ponce de León (great-granddaughter of King Alfonso IX of León), and sister of Alfonso Núñe
2 CONC z de Guzmán (ca 1300 – Gibraltar, 1342), Master of the Order of Santiago, married ca 1330 to Dona Dona María de La Cerda, 1st Lady of Villafranca de Valcárcel (ca 1290 –), without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor and Alfonso had ten children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lord of Aguilar de Campoo (1330 - 1338).
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lady of Trastamara (born 1330).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lord of Ledesma (1331 - 1343).
2 CONT
2 CONT Enrique Alfonso of Castile, 1st Count of Trastamara (1334 - 1379), in future king Henry II of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fadrique Alfonso of Castile, Master of the Order of Santiago and 1st Lord of Haro; (born 1335).
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernando Alfonso of Castile, 2nd Lord of Ledesma.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tello Alfonso of Castile, 2nd Lord of Aguilar de Campoo (born 1337).
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lord of Badajoz and Jerez de la Frontera (1341 - 1359).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Alfonso of Castile, 1st Count of Alburquerque (born 1342).
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro Alfonso of Castile (1345 - 1359).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_of_Guzman
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Guzman
