2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Navarre From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Navarre (1242–1295) was a daughter of Theobald I of Navarre and his third wife Margaret of Bourbon. Her siblings included, Theobald II of Navarre and Henry I of Navarre. She is also known as Beatrix of Champagne. Biogr
2 CONC aphy
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice was married to Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy, for political reasons. The couple married after the death of Hugh's first wife Yolande de Dreux. Hugh and Beatrice had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hugh, viscount of Avallon (1260–1288), married Marguerite of Burgundy, daughter of John I of Burgundy, Count Palatine.
2 CONT     * Margaret, Dame de Vitteaux (died 1300), married 1272 John de Chalon, Seigneur d'Arlay (1259–1316)
2 CONT     * Joan (died 1295)
2 CONT     * Beatrice, Lady of Grignon (ca.1260–1329), married Hugh XIII, count of La Marche
2 CONT     * Isabelle of Burgundy, Lady of Vieux-Château (1270–1323), married Rudolph I of Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice's son, Hugh did not succeed his father, since Hugh IV had another son, Robert, by his marriage to Yolande de Dreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her daughter, Isabella married Rudolph I of Germany. The marriage produced no children, since the bride was only fourteen and the groom was almost sixty-six. Isabella was younger than eight of Rudolph's children, by his first marr
2 CONC iage to Gertrude of Hohenburg and Judith, the ninth child was only one year younger than Isabella. Beatrice's son, Hugh married Margaret of Burgundy but died young and her other daughters were married off.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh IV died in 1271 and was succeeded by Robert. Beatrice died twenty four years later in 1295. External links
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Family tree
2 CONT     * Beatrice of Champagne Princess of Navarre
2 CONT
