1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elena of Bulgaria
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Elena of Bulgaria was daughter of Bulgarian Emperor Ivan Asen II and Empress Anna Maria of Hungary. Anna was originally named Mária.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elena was a Bulgarian princess and Empress of Nicaea. She was married to Theodore II Laskaris, who was Emperor of Nicaea, 1254–1258.
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Elena was the sister of Emperor Kaliman I of Bulgaria and Princess Tamara of Bulgaria. Her maternal grandfather and grandmother are King Andrew II of Hungary and Gertrude of Merania and her paternal grandfather and grandm
2 CONC other are Emperor Ivan Asen I of Bulgaria and Empress Elena of Bulgaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT First Elena was betrothed to Baldwin II of Courtenay, the last Latin emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elena and Theodore had three children: John IV Laskaris, Irene Doukaina Laskarina, who married Constantine Tikh of Bulgaria, and Maria Doukaina Laskarina, who married Nikephoros I Komnenos Doukas of Epirus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore died in 1259 and her son John Laskaris became Emperor of Nicaea. John was only seven years old and there were regency.
