2 CONT 1.         GUGLIELMO [III] (-after 7 May 1259).  Conte di Ventimiglia.  Guglielmo Conte di Ventimiglia “tant à son nom que de ses frères” signed a peace treaty with Charles d’Anjou Comte de Provence [Anjou-Capet] to whom he transf
2 CONC erred rights in property “qui avoient appartenu à Guillaume de Vintimille son père”, including “les châteaux et seigneuries de Saint Chenet, de Galps, de Tende, de la Brigue...et ce qu’il avoit à Roquebrune, Monaco...enfin général
2 CONC ement toute la comté de Vintimille”, in exchange for other properties in Provence, by charter dated 1257[738].  Saige, presumably citing the same document, notes that “Guillaume fils de Guillaume comte de Vintimille” transferred h
2 CONC is rights in the county of Ventimiglia by charter dated 19 Jan 1258, in terms similar to the 7 Apr 1258 charter quoted above under his first cousin Bonifazio[739].  The testament of Guglielmo Conte di Ventimiglia, dated 1259, name
2 CONC s his “six enfants...Guillaume III, Raymond, Rostan, Othon, Sibile et Berengere”[740].  Europäische Stammtafeln dates this document to “Grasse 7 May 1259”[741].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Guglielmo’s wife is not known.  Guglielmo [III] & his wife had six children: 
