2 CONT 2.         PIETRO Balbo (-after 21 Jan 1286).  Conte di Ventimiglia.  Conte Pietro Balbo “tant en son nom propre que de Guillaume-Pierre son autre frere et de Guillaume son neveu” made a treaty with Charles I King of Sicily, Comte
2 CONC  de Provence, settling disputes, dated 17 Mar 1278[755].  A charter dated 18 Dec 1285 records the renewal of an agreement between “dominum Philippum de Laveria militem dominum senescalliæ Provinciæ et Forcalquerii, nomine hæredum 
2 CONC quondam domini Karoli regis Siciliæ” and “dominum Petrum Balbum comitem Vintimilii nomine suo et nomine domini Guilelmi nepotis sui, don Iohannis et don Jayme et Ottonis nepotum ipsius et Belengariæ sororis ipsius domini Guilelmi”
2 CONC [756].  A charter dated 21 Jan 1286 records longstanding disputes between “dominum Karolum olim...Siciliæ regem” and “quondam G. P. et eius filios...Iohannem et Iacobum, Petrum Balbum et Guglielmum eius fratres, filios quondam G. 
2 CONC fratris dictorum domini Guilelmi Petri, et domini P. Balbis comitis Vintimilii” and renewed the peace agreement[757]. 
