2 CONT Translated from https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zayd_Abu_Zayd
2 CONT
2 CONT >[https://www.geni.com/people/Zayd-Abu-Zayd/6000000010671354763?through=6000000010669428008 Abu Zeit] married his daughter, Doña Alda Fernández, who probably brought the castle of Arenoso in dowry, with Don Eximén Pérez de Tarazon
2 CONC a, who was at the head of the Aragonese troop that constituted the military force of Abú Zayd; after this marriage the latter changed his name Tarazona to Arenós.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://an.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeit_Abu_Zeit cites 
2 CONT * (es) Barceló Torres, María del Carmen: El sayyid Abū Zayd: Príncipe musulmán, señor cristiano. Awraq. Estudios sobre el Mundo Árabe e Islámico Contemporáneo. (Madrid: Instituto de Cooperación con el Mundo Árabe, 1980).
2 CONT * (es) Burns, Robert I: Príncipe almohade y converso mudéjar: Nueva documentación sobre Abū Zayd. Sharq al-Andalus: Estudios árabes, 4 (Alacant : Universitat, 1987), pp. 109–122.
