2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Infopedia: Andrew II. 1175-1235. King (1205-35). Son of Bela III; succeeded Laszlo III. His extravagance and generosity brought financial troubles; forced to grant estates to nobles who reduced Hungary almost to anarchy
2 CONC . m. Gertrude of Meran, murdered (1213) by nobles. Set out with large army on crusade to Holy Land (1217); sailed to Acre, but expedition failed. On return nobles extorted from him (1222) the Golden Bull, which limited the monarch
2 CONC y, granted people annual assembly, and preserved rights of feudal nobles; during his reign Teutonic Knights expelled from Hungary (1225). Father of St. Elizabeth of Hungary. 
2 CONT
