2 CONT THE ROYAL ANCESTRY CONNECTION TO THE TILLINGHAST LINE
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted by: Elton L. Powell (ID *****3093) 	Date: August 30, 2002 at 18:56:48
2 CONT
2 CONT   	of 329
2 CONT
2 CONT For many years there has been an effort of some of the Tillinghast descendents to find a blood connection to British
2 CONT
2 CONT Royalty. Unfortunately for some of these they obviously found the earliest effort to make a Royal connection to King Edward III which in all cases has turned out to be WRONG. This effort had been put forth by a Dr.Wiess in a set o
2 CONC f volumns called, "The American Genealogist", 'TAGS, if you will. The Doctor later admitted his error and stated that there was no provable connection through a Mrs Tichbourne. As I have stated in other messages, I have not found 
2 CONC any marriage between a Tillinghast and a Tichbourne. Right now there are only some 100 messages on this Tillinghast Message board and all could be read in a reasonable length of time. Pay particular attention to these.
2 CONT
2 CONT #'s 25 / 29 / 66 / 68 / 69 / 82 / 94 / 97 / & 99. I am not the expert but I can report on what I have found and I have already passed along this info to others; Mss.Debbie Richardson; Mr.Todd Lawrence; etc. And I stated on where I
2 CONC  found it. But there IS a Tillinghast connection to the Royal
2 CONT
2 CONT Blood of Britain and a Mss Vaughn in Britain researched it.
2 CONT
2 CONT It goes through the wife of the 1st Pardon Tillinghast, the beer barrel maker,[cooper if you will].
2 CONT
2 CONT Kg EDWARD I; 1239-1307 -M- Princess MARGARITTE, dau. / Kg. Philip III of France. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS de BROTHERTON, Earl of Norfolk. 1301-1338 -M- ALICE
2 CONT
2 CONT de HALLES, dau./Sir Roger de Halles. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT MARGARET PLANTEGENET, Duchess of Norfolk; -M- JOHN, 4th Baron Seagrave. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT ELIZABETH SEAGRAVE, dau.& heir. -M- JOHN, 4th Baron Mowbray
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT ELEANOR MOWBRAY; -M- JOHN, 5th Baron de Welles. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT EDO de WELLES; -M- MAUDE de GREYSTOCK, dau./Ralph, 5th /Baron de Greystock. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR LIONEL de WELLES; 6th Baron de Welles, K. G.{Knight of the Garter]. -M- CECILIA,[or Joan] DAU./ROBERT WATERTON of
2 CONT
2 CONT Methley. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT ELEANOR de WELLES, -M- THOMAS, Lord Hoo, K.G./ Chancellor to France. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT ANNA de HOO, dau. & co-heir; -M- Sir ROGER de COPLEY,[15th in descent from King Athelred II. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT ANN COPLEY; -M- WILLIAM LUSHER, Lord of Rodsell Manor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT GEORGE LUSHER, Gentleman, -M- Alice...........Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT ANNE LUSHER; -M- Sir RICHARD LECHFORD,Knight, of Shellwood Manor in Leigh, Surrey County. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT SARAH LECHFORD, -M- Rev. BENJAMIN BROWNE, Vicar of Ifiel County, Sussex. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT SARAH BROWNE, bn.1600- dd. ? ; -M- PARDON TILLINGHAST, yeoman and cooper of Streat, Sussez County, bn. 1601
2 CONT
2 CONT Notice that this connection is made through Sarah Browne, the emigrant's mother. The name, Tillinghast , has not always been spelled this way. And the earliest that I have found it even in its earliest forms,[like Tyllynghrst, etc
2 CONC .] is about 800 AD. At a later date I will give what info I have on earlier antecedents but I never found a continual'bloodline'
