2 CONC t yet been identified.  She was accused and convicted of adultery, imprisoned at Château-Gaillard 26 Aug 1319-21 May 1321, then repudiated by Charles on the grounds of consanguinity.  She became a nun at the Abbaye de Maubuisson a
2 CONC fter her repudiation.  m secondly (Provins, Seine-et-Marne 21 Sep 1322) MARIE de Luxembourg, daughter of Emperor HEINRICH VII Comte de Luxembourg & his wife Marguerite de Brabant (1305-Issoudun, Indre Mar 1324, bur Montargis, Loir
2 CONC et, église des religieuses de Saint-Dominique).  Consecrated Queen at Paris Sainte-Chapelle 15 May 1323.  She died in childbirth after falling out of the bottom of the coach which was driving her and her husband to a meeting with 
