2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles,_Count_of_Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Valois (12 March 1270 – 16 December 1325) was the fourth son of Philip III of France and Isabella of Aragon.[1] He was a member of the House of Capet and founded the House of Valois. In 1284, he was created Count of Val
2 CONC ois (as Charles I) by his father and, in 1290, received the title of Count of Anjou from his marriage to Margaret of Anjou.[2]
