1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: France [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAPET.htm#JeanneValoisdied1363 Capetian Kings]
2 CONT * 8. '''JEANNE de Valois''' ([1304]-Château-Gaillard 9 Jul 1363, bur Paris, église des Augustins). 
2 CONT * The Continuatio of the Chronicle of Guillaume de Nangis records the marriage in 1316 of "Robertus Attrebatensis comitissæ nepos ex fratre" and "filiam comitis Valesii"[906]. 
2 CONT * She was called Madame d'Artois. 
2 CONT * She encouraged her husband to revolt, the king her brother arrested her in 1334. She was imprisoned at Château-Gaillard, where she died many years later. 
2 CONT * ['''Betrothed''' (1308) to '''GUY Comte de Blois''', son of HUGUES [II] de Châtillon Comte de Blois & his wife Beatrix de Flandre.] 
2 CONT * '''Betrothed''' (1313) to '''CHARLES di Tarento''' Despot of Epirus, son of PHILIPPE of Sicily Principe di Tarento [Anjou-Capet] & his first wife Thamar Angelina Komnene Dukaina of Epirus ([1296]-killed in battle Montecatini, be
2 CONC tween Pistoia and Lucca 29 Aug 1315). 
2 CONT * '''m''' (1318) '''ROBERT d'Artois''' Comte de Beaumont-le-Roger, son of PHILIPPE d’Artois Seigneur de Conches & his wife Blanche de Bretagne (1287-[Brest], Brittany end-Oct 1342, bur London, St Paul's). He was banished from Fran
2 CONC ce and his assets confiscated 19 Mar 1332.
