1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gaston VII of Béarn
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1245 and 1250 Gaston married Mathe de Matha (or Amata of Mastas; died 1270/3), Viscountess of Marsan, daughter of Boson de Mathe, lord of Cognac, and Petronilla of Bigorre. The couple had four children, all daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance (died 1310), succeeded in Marsan and Bigorre. Married firstly, on 23 March 1260, to the Aragonese infante Alfonso, son of James the Conqueror, who died 26 March; married secondly, on 15 May 1269, to Henry of Almaine, son
2 CONC  of Richard of Cornwall; and married thirdly, in 1279, to Aymon II of Geneva
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, succeeded in Béarn. Married, in 1252, to Roger-Bernard III de Foix
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathe, married Geraud VI of Armagnac in 1260
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillelme (or Guillemette; died 1309), affianced in 1270 to Sancho IV of Castile, annulled 1281; married, in 1291, to the Aragonese infante Peter (1275–1296), son of Peter the Great
2 CONT
2 CONT Widowered, Gaston married again on 2 April 1273 to Beatrice (c. 1237–1310), daughter of Peter II of Savoy and Agnès de Faucigny, and widow of Guigues VII of Viennois
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]
