1 NOTE KING OF FRANCE 1226-1270 (ACCEDED 11/8/1226, AND WAS LATER CONSECRATED AT RHEIMS
2 CONT 11/29/1226); SAINT; GAVE THE COUNTSHIP OF ANJOU TO HIS BROTHER, WHO BECAME
2 CONT CHARLES I OF NAPLES; LEADER OF THE 6TH CRUSADE (1228-1229) WITH FREDERICK II;
2 CONT LEADER OF THE 7TH CRUSADE (1248-1254) WITH BROTHER CHARLES; LEADER OF THE 8TH
2 CONT CRUSADE (1270-1291) WITH BROTHER CHARLES & EDWARD I, KING OF ENGLAND (DIED OF
2 CONT THE PLAGUE WHILE IN CARTHAGE EARLY IN CRUSADE)
1 NOTE St. Loius IX Capet
2 CONT h t t p : / / t r e e s . a n c e s t r y . c o m / r d ? f = i m a g e&guid=ba79c0a5-72f7-4012-a8d1-e85f2eaafe6b&tid=312040&pid=-1911824731
1 NOTE He was a Crusader King. He was canonized on 11 Aug 1297 by Pope Boniface VIII.
1 NOTE Armorial Général de France: Les SABRAN
