1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Agnes of France, Duchess of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes of France (c. 1260 - December 19, 1327) was the youngest daughter of Louis IX of France and Marguerite Berenger of Provence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes had ten older siblings, including Philip III of France and Robert, Count of Clermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Robert II, Duke of Burgundy and became the mother of seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh V, Duke of Burgundy (1282–1315).
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche (1288–1348), married Edward of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite (1290- 1315), married king Louis X of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (Jeanne) (ca.1290–1348), married count of Maine and Valois, king Philip VI of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudes IV, Duke of Burgundy (1295–1350).
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, King of Thessalonica (1297–1316), married Matilda of Hainaut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, count of Tonnerre (1302–1334), married Joanna, heiress of Tonnerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnes_of_France,_Duchess_of_Burgundy
2 CONT
