1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalmau_VII_de_Rocabert%C3%AD
2 CONT
2 CONT Dalmau VII of Rocabertí and Urgell (? - 1324) was Viscount of Rocabertí between 1309 and 1324 . He was a military man and trusted man of James II and one of the main actors in the Aragonese conquest of Sardinia , advancing the bul
2 CONC k of the expedition with 200 knights and 2,000 infantry with his uncle Guerau de Rocabertí i Desfar [1] to help Hugh II of Arborea , taking Quart and besieging the Castel di Castro during which he lost his life. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Beatriu de Cabrenys , daughter of Bernat Hug de Cabrenys , who contributed the barony of Cabrenys to the Rocabertí patrimony . From this marriage were born:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jofre V de Rocabertí , heir to the viscounty Guillem Galceran de Rocabertí , married to Maria d'Arborea , daughter of Judge Hug II d'Arborea . He started the Rocabertí de Cabrenys branch . Timbor de Rocabertí , married to Maria IV
2 CONC  of Arborea , son and heir of judge Hug II of Arborea
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From fmgMedlands 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         DALMAU [IV] de Rocabertí (-1324).  The genealogical table of the Rocaberti family in the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana names “Dalmau VII †1324” as son of Jofre [IV].  The primary source which confirms this information have
2 CONC  not been identified.  Vescomte de Rocabertí.  Zurita names “don Dalmau Vizconde de Rocabertí, don Guerau de Rocabertí su tio..” among the leading nobles in Catalonia in 1323[1647]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  m ---.  The primary sources which confirm the name(s) of Dalmau’s wife/wives have not been identified.  The genealogical table of the Rocaberti family in the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana names them “1 Ermessenda de Cartellà, 2 Beat
2 CONC riu de Serralonga baronessa de Cabrenys, senyora de Maçanet, Reiners, Hostoles i Rocacorba”.  Dalmau [IV] & his wife had children: 
2 CONT           i)          JOFRE [V] de Rocabertí (-1342).  The genealogical table of the Rocaberti family in the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana names “Jofre V †1342” as son of Dalmau.  The primary source which confirms this information ha
2 CONC ve not been identified.  Vescomte de Rocabertí. 
