1 NAME Jofre VI de Rocabertí, vescomte de Rocaberti (1392-1403)
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1403
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jofre (VI) of Rocabertí and Fenollet was viscount of Rocabertí between 1392 and 1403 .
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Viscount Felip Dalmau I of Rocabertí and Esclarmonda de Fenollet . He was chamberlain of John I of Aragon and went to Sicily with his father in 1392 on an expedition organized by Infante Martí , Duke of Montblanc
2 CONC , where his father died and he quickly returned to his domains to take possession.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of King Joan, he was also a chamberlain of King Martí and served him at the beginning of his reign to expel the warriors of the count of Foix who invaded the north of the Principality. In 1398 the king entrusted hi
2 CONC m with the command of a flock of punishments that was to go to Barbaria and recover some sacred wafers that had been stolen from Torreblanca by pirates. This expedition took the place of Tedel·lís , in the kingdom of Tremissèn . B
2 CONC ack in Catalonia, the flock was quite ruined by storms and the king asked him to go to Avignon to help Pope Benedict XIII , but as Tarascó the waters were low they could not get there.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1402 his brother-in-law, Pere II d'Empúries , married Joana de Rocabertí, died . Joana remained heiress of the county of Empúries and, alternatively, Jofre, but King Martí prevented this inheritance and in return offered other 
2 CONC possessions to the Rocabertís . In addition, the untimely death of Jofre in 1403 meant that these rights could not be claimed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jofre married Isabel Ferrandis of Híxar , daughter of the Aragonese nobleman Pedro Ferrandis of Híxar descendant of James I . From this marriage was born Dalmau VIII of Rocabertí , heir to the viscounty. When his father died he wa
2 CONC s very young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT Santiago Sobrequés i Vidal, Els barons de Catalunya , Barcelona, ​​Teide, 1957.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From fmgMedlands 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         JOFRE [VI] de Rocabertí (-1403).  His parentage is confirmed by Zurita’s reference to his betrothal, quoted below.  He succeeded his father in 1392 as Vescomte de Rocabertí.  Zurita records the death in 1392 in the king
2 CONC dom of Sicily of “don Felipe Dalmao Vizconde de Rocabertí” and the succession of “don Iofre su hijo”[1656].  Betrothed ([1385/86]) to doña MARÍA Fadrique de Aragón, daughter of don LUIS Fadrique de Aragón Count of Salona & his wif
2 CONC e Helena Asanine Kantakouzene ([1370]-murdered Adrianople 1395).  She succeeded her father [1381/82] as Ctss of Salona, Lady of Siderokastron, under the regency of her mother.  Zurita records that her widowed mother arranged the m
2 CONC arriage of her daughter “Maria Federico Cantacuzin” and “[el] hijo del Vizconde [...don Felipe Dalmao Vizconde de Rocabertí]”[1657].  If Zurita is correct, this betrothal is probably dated to [1385/86].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (1393) ISABEL Fernandez de Hijar, daughter of PEDRO Fernández de Hijar Barón de Hijar & his third wife Isabel de Mesia (-before 1410).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.  
