1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chapter 3.    KINGS of NAVARRE 1234-1305 (CHAMPAGNE)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAVARRE.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT THIBAUT de Champagne, son of THIBAUT III Comte de Champagne & his wife Infanta doña Blanca de Navarra (Pamplona 3 May 1201-Pamplona 8 Jul 1253, bur Pamplona).  Villehardouin records that the wife of Comte Thibaut "had borne him a 
2 CONC little daughter and was about to bear a son" when her husband died[615].  He succeeded his father in 1201 as THIBAUT IV Comte de Champagne et de Brie.  
2 CONT
2 CONT King Teobaldo I had four illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 8. ELIDA de Navarra (-[1238/42]). The marriage contract of "Petrus Ferrandus dominus civitatis S. Mariæ de Alvarracin…filium meum Alvar Petriz" (substituting "secundum filium meum Petrum Ferrandi…tertium filium meum…Garciam Orti
2 CONC z") and "domino Th…Navarræ, Campaniæ et Briæ comite palatino…Ælidis filiæ eiusdem…regis Navarræ" is dated Mar 1237[664]. Betrothed (contract Mar 1237) ÁLVARO Pérez de Azagra Señor de Albarracín, son of PEDRO Fernández de Azagra & 
2 CONC his wife ---.
2 CONT * 9. INES de Navarra . Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by a charter dated 15 Jul 1243 under which "D. Alvar Periz" donated the pueblo of Santa Olalla to "mi muger doña Ignis filla del rey de Navarra", confirmed by "D. Ped
2 CONC ro Ferrandez Dazagra vasaillo de Sancta Maria é seinnor de Albarracin"[665]. m (before 15 Jul 1243) as his second wife, ÁLVARO Pérez de Azagra Señor de Albarracín, son of PEDRO Fernández de Azagra & his wife --- .
2 CONT * 10. GUILLERMO de Navarra ([1225 or after]-30 Dec before 1267). The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records that "comes Campaniensis Theobaldus" had "filium nomine Guillelmum bastardum", dating the event to "quo tempore r
2 CONC ex"[666]. As the same passage records the arrival of Thibaut in Navarre to join his uncle in 1225, it is assumed that "quo tempore rex" is intended to mean "during the time his uncle was king" rather than "while he [Thibaut] was k
2 CONC ing". The marriage dates of the illegitimate daughters of Thibaut indicate that they must have been born before his accession, which also suggests that this interpretation of the phrase in the Chronicle is correct. The Chronicle a
2 CONC lso adds in the same passage that "episcopus Pampelone" was "frater uterinus eiusdem bastardi", giving a clue to the identity of the mother of Guillermo. A priest.
2 CONT * 11. BERENGUELA de Navarra . Prioress of San Pedro de Ribas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
