1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theobald_II,_Duke_of_Lorraine Theobald II, Duke of Lorraine From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search 	This article does not cite any references or sources. Plea
2 CONC se help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced material may be challenged and removed. (September 2008)
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald II (French: Thiébaud or Thiébaut) (1263 – May 13, 1312) was the duke of Lorraine from 1303 to his death. He was the son and successor of Frederick III and Margaret, daughter of King Theobald I of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1298, he took part in the Battle of Göllheim, near Speyer, in which the king of Germany, Adolph, was killed fighting his rival, Albert of Habsburg. Theobald was on Albert' side, despite the history of support for the legitimate
2 CONC  emperors (which Adolph aspired to be) in the history of his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1302, he was at war helping the king of France, Philip IV, married to his cousin Joan I of Navarre. He was at the Battle of the Golden Spurs at Kortrijk, where the Flemings defeated the French chivalry under Robert II of Artois
2 CONC . He was present also at the Battle of Mons-en-Pévèle in 1304, where the French king personally led the army in a less decisive battle. He, along with John II, Duke of Brabant, and Amadeus V, Count of Savoy, was sent to negotiate 
2 CONC peace with Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1305, he was at Lyon, at the crowning of Pope Clement V. When Clement imposed a tax, a tenth-part, on the clergy and charged the duke to collect it, Theobald successfully met the opposition of Renaud de Bar, bishop of Metz. [ed
2 CONC it] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1278 Isabella (1263-1326), lady of Rumigny, daughter of Hugh, lord of Rumigny, and Philippine d'Oulche. They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Frederick (1282 † 1329), his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT     * Matthias (d.c.1330), lord of Darney, Boves, Blainville, and Florennes
2 CONT     * Hugh, his successor in Rumigny, Martigny, and Aubenton
2 CONT     * Mary, married (1324) Guy de Châtillon (d.1362), lord of La Fère-en-Tardenois
2 CONT     * Margaret († 1348), married (c.1311) Guy de Dampierre, count of Zeeland (d.1311)
2 CONT     * Isabella (d.1353), married Érard de Bar (d.1337), lord of Pierrepont
2 CONT     * Philippine, nun
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] See also
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Dukes of Lorraine family tree
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by Frederick III 	Duke of Lorraine 1303-1312 	Succeeded by Frederick IV This page was last modified on 24 December 2009 at 04:31.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Theobald II, Duke of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald II (French: Thiébaud or Thiébaut) (1263 – May 13, 1312) was the duke of Lorraine from 1303 to his death. He was the son and successor of Frederick III and Margaret, daughter of King Theobald I of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1298, he took part in the Battle of Göllheim, near Speyer, in which the king of Germany, Adolph, was killed fighting his rival, Albert of Habsburg. Theobald was on Albert' side, despite the history of support for the legitimate
2 CONC  emperors (which Adolph aspired to be) in the history of his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1302, he was at war helping the king of France, Philip IV, married to his cousin Joan I of Navarre. He was at the Battle of the Golden Spurs at Kortrijk, where the Flemings defeated the French chivalry under Robert II of Artois
2 CONC . He was present also at the Battle of Mons-en-Pévèle in 1304, where the French king personally led the army in a less decisive battle. He, along with John II, Duke of Brabant, and Amadeus V, Count of Savoy, was sent to negotiate 
2 CONC peace with Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1305, he was at Lyon, at the crowning of Pope Clement V. When Clement imposed a tax, a tenth-part, on the clergy and charged the duke to collect it, Theobald successfully met the opposition of Renaud de Bar, bishop of Metz.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1278 Isabella (1263-1326), lady of Rumigny, daughter of Hugh, lord of Rumigny, and Philippine d'Oulche. They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick (1282 † 1329), his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias (d.c.1330), lord of Darney, Boves, Blainville, and Florennes
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh, his successor in Rumigny, Martigny, and Aubenton
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary, married (1324) Guy de Châtillon (d.1362), lord of La Fère-en-Tardenois
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret († 1348), married (c.1311) Guy de Dampierre, count of Zeeland (d.1311)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella (d.1353), married Érard de Bar (d.1337), lord of Pierrepont
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippine, nun
