1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Genealogy 
2 CONT ==== Chapter 11.  FAMILY of PEDRO ANSÚREZ
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL.htm#AnsurDiazdied1047B
2 CONT
2 CONT ANSUR Díaz, son of conde DIEGO Fernández de Saldaña & his wife Marina --- (-after 29 Sep 1047).  “...Fernando Didaz comes...Ansur Didaz, Gomez Didaz...” subscribed the charter dated 17 Feb 1035 under which King Vermudo III recogni
2 CONC sed the church of Palencia and made donations[904].  "Fernando Didaz comes…Assur Diaz, Gomez Didaz" subscribed the charter dated 1036 under which Vermudo III King of León donated property[905].  “...comite Fredinando Didaz, Asurz 
2 CONC Didaz” witnessed the charter dated 24 May 1038 under which Fernando I King of Castile granted “castellum...Vierbele” to “Garcia Eneconis”[906].  Conde [Apr/Oct] 1042.  "Assur Diaz et uxor mea Iusta" donated property in León to Leó
2 CONC n Cathedral by charter dated 29 Sep 1047[907]. 
2 CONT * [m firstly ---.  The name of Ansur´s first wife is not known.  Ansur & his [first/third] wife had three children: 
2 CONT **1.         PEDRO Ansúrez (-9 Sep 1119).  The Chronicon Mundi of Lucas Tudensis names "tres fratres nobiles…Petrus Ansuri, Gundisaluus Ansuri et Fernanduss Ansuri"[916].  Mayordomo of Alfonso VI King of León 24 Jul 1067 to 3 Sep 
2 CONC 1067.  Conde [1071].  -        see below. 
2 CONT * m [secondly] --- Ovéquiz, daughter of OVECO Téllez & his wife Elvira - Ansur & his [second] wife had one child: 
2 CONT **2.         GONZALO Ansúrez (-after 1075). 
2 CONT * [m thirdly ---.  The identity of the mother of Ansur´s son, Fernando, has not been ascertained with certainty. Ansur & his [third] wife had one child: 
2 CONT **3.         FERNANDO Ansúrez (-after 20 Jan [1096/98]).
2 CONT *m [fourthly] '''JUSTA Fernández''', daughter of [conde FERNANDO Flaínez & his wife Elvira Peláez] (-after 29 Mar 1085). Ansur & his [fourth] wife had one child:
2 CONT **4.         DIEGO Ansúrez (-18 Jul 1084, bur León Cathedral). Diego & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT ***a)         ELVIRA Díaz (-18 Jul --). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Ansúrez Wikipedia] > '''Pedro Ansúrez''' (floruit 1065–1117;[2] died probably 9 September 1118[3]) was a Castilian nobleman, count of Liébana, Saldaña and Carrión in the closing decades of 
2 CONC the eleventh century and the opening decades of the twelfth. He is considered the founder and first lord of Valladolid. Pedro was a descendant of the Beni Gómez family of Castilian nobility, the son of Ansur Díaz, by his first wif
2 CONC e, whose name is unknown.[4] His grandfather, Diego Fernández, was a count of Saldaña and Carrión. 
