2 CONT 3.         OBERTO (-after 4 Oct 1234).  Conte di Ventimiglia.  Emmanuele Conte di Ventimiglia was present when “son frère Obert ou Aubert comte de Vintimille” sold “la moitié de la jurisdiction des terres de Châteauneuf...” by cha
2 CONC rter dated 2 Jul 1217[729].  “Obertus comes Vintimilii et dominus Baaluchi filius quondam domini Guillelmi comitis de Vintimilio” sold one third of “castri...Carpaxii” to Genoa by charter dated 4 Oct 1234[730].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 28 Jul 1217) GUILLEMETTE de Marseille, daughter of [RAYMOND GEOFFROY [II] Vicomte de Marseille & his wife Ixmille Marquise].  Robert records that a document dated 28 Jul 1217 acknowledges payment of part of the dow
2 CONC ry for the marriage of “Guillemette fille de Raymond Gaufridi Vicomte de Marseille” and “Obert Comte de Vintimille”[731].  Assuming that this information is accurate, the chronology appears to suggest that Guillemette was the daug
2 CONC hter of Raymond Geoffroy [II].  Oberto & his wife had two children: 
