1 NOTE Rey de Castilla
1 NOTE Conde de Trastámara, Lemos y Sarria; Rey de Castilla y León (1369-1379)
1 NOTE Henry II (of Castile and León) (1333?-79), known as Henry (Enrique) of 
2 CONT Trastamara, king of Castile and León (1369-79), born in Seville. He was 
2 CONT the illegitimate son of Alfonso XI of Castile, who made him count of 
2 CONT Trastamara. After the accession of Alfonso's legitimate son, Peter the 
2 CONT Cruel, to the throne of Castile and León in 1350, Henry fled to France. 
2 CONT With an army of mercenaries financed by the kings of France and Aragon, 
2 CONT Henry invaded Castile in 1366 and drove Peter from the throne. Edward, 
2 CONT prince of Wales, intervened for Peter, however, and defeated Henry at 
2 CONT Nájera in 1367. Henry defeated and killed Peter in 1369, becoming king and 
2 CONT continuing his alliance with Charles V of France in the Hundred Years' 
2 CONT War. In 1372 his navy destroyed an English fleet off La Rochelle. He was 
2 CONT succeeded by his son John I.
1 NOTE "OF TRASTAMARA"; KING OF ARAGON 1369-1379; ILLEGITIMATE
1 NOTE KING OF CASTILE
1 NOTE Enrique II de Trastámara, primer rey de Castilla de la dinastía Trastámara, llamado el Fratricida o el de las Mercedes.
2 CONT Miniatura fechada en 1594
2 CONT Miniatura fechada en 1594
