1 NOTE {geni:about_me} unknown uncertain presumed illegitimate homonymous half-sister of  
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Mar%C3%ADa-de-Portugal-reina-consorte-de-Castilla-y-Le%C3%B3n/6000000000124890646  ?
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''María Alfonso de Portugal''', que según algunos genealogistas españoles como Francisco Fernández de Béthencourt​ y Luis de Salazar y Castro​ era hija ilegítima del [https://www.geni.com/people/Afonso-IV-o-Ousado-rei-de-Portuga
2 CONC l/6000000000111086524  rey Alfonso IV de Portugal] y de una [https://www.geni.com/people/Catalina-Mart%C3%ADnez-de-Torres/4674507057700018269  dama de nombre desconocido],​ aunque no aportan ninguna prueba que demuestre esa filiac
2 CONC ión. ​ 
2 CONT *''Pero la mayoría de los historiadores portugueses modernos afirman rotundamente que [https://www.geni.com/people/Afonso-IV-o-Ousado-rei-de-Portugal/6000000000111086524  Alfonso IV de Portugal] no tuvo ningún hijo ilegítimo, y ar
2 CONC gumentan que ello pudo ser debido a las malas relaciones que tuvo con sus propios hermanastros,​ o debido a las buenas y armoniosas relaciones que siempre mantuvo con su esposa, la [https://www.geni.com/people/Beatriz-de-Castela-r
2 CONC ainha-consorte-de-Portugal/6000000010829929660  reina Beatriz de Castilla].​ Sin embargo, las importantes donaciones que le han sido hechas prueban la pertenencia a la Casa Real de Portugal, por via ilegítima, lo que parece confir
2 CONC mado por la falta de elementos a su respecho, podendo tratarse de una hija tardía de [https://www.geni.com/people/Dinis-I-o-Justo-rei-de-Portugal/6000000000109941736  Dinis I ].''
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_de_Valencia#Or%C3%ADgenes_familiares 
2 CONT # https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hernando_de_Valencia#Or%C3%ADgenes_familiares
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fernando_Alfonso_de_Valencia#Matrimonio_y_descendencia
2 CONT
2 CONT Most modern Portuguese historians categorically state that Alfonso IV of Portugal had no illegitimate sons,109 and argue that this could be due to the bad relations he had with his own half-brothers,110 or due to the good and harm
2 CONC onious relations he always maintained with his wife, Queen Beatrix of Castile.111 112 o But according to most Spanish genealogists, such as Francisco Fernández de Bethencourt113 and Luis Bartolomé de Salazar y Castro,114 115 Ferna
2 CONC ndo Alfonso de Valencia married María Alfonso de Portugal,2 who would have been the illegitimate daughter of King Alfonso IV of Portugal4 and a lady of unknown name,116 although they did not provide any proof to prove that filiati
2 CONC on.p And according to some of the historians mentioned above, María Alfonso de Portugal was lady of Miranda do Douro, Mirandela, Vila Flor, Torre de Moncorvo and Bemposta and her father gave her 400,000maravedís as a dowry for her
2 CONC  late from Dinis I. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And as a result of his marriage to Fernando Alfonso de Valencia, the following children would have been born:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Hernando de Valencia (d. 1425). He was the eldest son of Fernando Alfonso de Valencia118 and became alderman of Zamora.114 12 But he renounced his property and professed as a religious of the Order of San Jerónimo4 in the monast
2 CONC ery of Guadalupe,107 being also the most outstanding of the founders of the monastery of Our Lady of Montamarta.119
2 CONT # Juan de Valencia (d. after 1427). Fuemariscal de Castilla120 2 and warden of the Alcázares de Zamora.107
2 CONT # Alfonso of Valencia. He was alderman of Zamora and member of the Regency Council during the minority of Henry III of Castile.107 And he married Mencía de Quesada, who was the daughter of Pedro Díaz de Quesada, lord of Garcíez, a
2 CONC nd Juana de Cárcamo.121 107 And after his death his widow married Egas Venegas, III
