1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20EMPERORS.htm#PierreIEmpdied1219B MedLands]
2 CONT
2 CONT SIBYLLE de Courtenay ([1210 or after?]-Fontevraud [after 1223?]).  She became a nun at Fontevraud Abbey.  Bouchet states that “Sibylle de Courtenay...fut religieuse à Fontevraut” adding that “son père fit une donation en sa faveur
2 CONC ...ce qui fut confirmé par son frère Philippes de Courtenay Marquis de Namur l´an 1223 au mois de Mars” but does not provide the citation reference for either document[107].  It is not clear from Bouchet´s paragraph whether Sibyll
2 CONC e was still alive at the date of her brother´s confirmation of the donation.  The necrology of Fontevraud records the death of “Sibylla...virgo apud Fontem-Ebrardi ætatis XIII annorum filia comitis Autissiodorensis et Yolendis de 
2 CONC Flandrie”; Bouchet adds the date “1223” in the margin but it is unclear whether the necrology records the year.
2 CONT
2 CONT .
