1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Constance Arpád=
2 CONT  (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #104646, d. 1240
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=19 Nov 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT      '''Constance Arpád''' is the daughter of '''Béla III Arpád, King of Hungary''' and '''Agnes de Châtillon'''. (2) She married '''Premysl Ottokar I, King of Bohemia''', son of Vladislav I, King of Bohemia and Judith von Thuring
2 CONC e, in 1198. (3) 
2 CONT
2 CONT *She died in 1240. (3)
2 CONT *Children of Constance Arpád and Premysl Ottokar I, King of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT # Anne of Bohemia+ (3) b. 1204, d. 1265
2 CONT # Wenceslas I, King of Bohemia+ (3) b. 1205, d. 1253
2 CONT # Wladislaw, Margrave of Moravia (3) b. 1207, d. 1227
2 CONT # Premysl, Margrave of Moravia (3) b. 1209, d. 1239
2 CONT # Agnes 'the Saint' of Bohemia (3) b. 1211, d. 1282
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10465.htm#i104646
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Konstancia királyi hercegnő''' 2010. január 14. '''Konstancia''' (Esztergom, 1180. február 17. – Tisnovitz, 1240. december 4.) cseh királyné, '''I. Ottokár cseh király''' felesége.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''III. Béla magyar király''' és '''Châtillon Anna''' másodszülött leányaként született. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Testvérei===
2 CONT *'''Imre''' magyar király, 
2 CONT *'''Margit''', 
2 CONT *'''II. András''', 
2 CONT *'''Salamon''', 
2 CONT *'''István''', 
2 CONT *'''Ágnes'''. 1199-ben férjhez ment I. Ottokár cseh királyhoz miután az közeli vérrokonság ürügyén elvált első feleségétől, Adelhaidtól. A házasságkötéskor megkapta a lundenburgi területet. 1230-ban özvegy lett, ekkor próbált béké
2 CONC t teremteni két fia, Vencel és Przemysl közt. Végül csak Vencel lett a cseh uralkodó. Nagyon kedves, adakozó, jólelkű volt. A csehek a béke angyalaként emlegették Konstanciát, a Przemysl uralkodóház ősanyját.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Gyermekei / Potomci (Česky)==
2 CONT
2 CONT *-1) Vratiszlav - fiatalon meghalt / 1- Vratislav (1200 – 1201?)
2 CONT *-2) Jutta - Bernát karintiai herceg felesége / 2- Judita Přemyslovna († 1230), korutanská vévodkyně∞ 1213 Bernard II. Sponheimský (Korutanský)
2 CONT *-3) Anna - II. Henrik lengyel fejedelem felesége / 3- Anna Lehnická (1204 - 1265), polská kněžna ∞ Jindřich II. Pobožný"
2 CONT *- ) / 4- Anežka
2 CONT *-4) I. Vencel cseh király *felesége?!* / 5- Václav I. (1205 - 1253), český král ∞ 1224 Kunhuta Štaufská
2 CONT *-5) *Kunigunda: Fülöp német király lánya?!
2 CONT * -) / 6- Vladislav (1207 - 1227), markrabě moravský
2 CONT *-6) Przemysl - morva örgróf / 7- Přemysl (1209 - 1239), markrabě moravský ∞ Markéta z Meranu
2 CONT *-7) Ulászló - fiatalom meghalt / 
2 CONT *-8) Prágai Szent Ágnes - Klarisszaapátnő / 9- Anežka Česká (1211 – 1282)
2 CONT *- / 8- Vilemína Česká (1210 - 1281)?
2 CONT
2 CONT *Konstancia 1236-ban a csehországi Tisnovitzi kolostorba lépett. Ott halt meg 1240. december 4-én. Ott temették el.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konstancia_kir%C3%A1lyi_hercegn%C5%91
2 CONT
2 CONT http://cs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konstancie_Uhersk%C3%A1
2 CONT
2 CONT English:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Constance of Hungary=
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Tenure 1199-1230 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Ottokar I of Bohemia 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Issue 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Wenceslaus I of Bohemia
2 CONT # Anna of Bohemia
2 CONT # Saint Agnes of Bohemia
2 CONT * Father Béla III of Hungary 
2 CONT * Mother Agnes of Antioch 
2 CONT * Born c. 1180 Hungary 
2 CONT * Died 6 December 1240 (aged c. 60) Tichnowitz, Moravia 
2 CONT * Burial Cloister Tichnowitz 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Constance was a daughter of Béla III of Hungary and his first wife Agnes of Antioch. Her older siblings included Emeric of Hungary, Margaret of Hungary and Andrew II of Hungary. Two other siblings, Solomon and Stephen, are mentio
2 CONC ned in the "Europäische Stammtafeln: Stammtafeln zur Geschichte der Europäischen Staaten" (1878) by Detlev Schwennicke. They reportedly died young. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT *Her paternal grandparents were Géza II of Hungary and Euphrosyne of Kiev. [3] Her maternal grandparents were Raynald of Chatillon and Constance of Antioch (joint princes of Antioch). [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and children===
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1199, Ottokar I divorced his first wife, Adelheid of Meissen, on grounds of consanguinity. He married Constance later in the same year. They had nine children.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance is regularly noted as a co-donator with her husband in various documents of his reign. Her petitions to her husband for various donations are also recorded. She is considered to have sold the city Boleráz to her nephew B
2 CONC éla IV of Hungary. In 1247, Béla conferred said city to the nuns of Trnava. An epistle by which Constance supposedly grants freedom to the cities of Břeclav and Olomouc is considered a false document. The same epistle grants lands
2 CONC  in Ostrovany to the monastery of St. Stephen of Hradište. Another epistle has Constance settling "honorable Teutonic men" (viros honestos Theutunicos) in the city of Hodonín and is also considered a forgery. [5] On 15 January 123
2 CONC 0, Ottokar I died and their son Wenceslaus succeeded him. Constance survived her husband by a decade. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1231, Pope Gregory IX set Constance and her dowry possessions under the protection of the Holy See. His letter to Constance clarifies said possessions to include the provinces of Břeclav (Brecyzlaviensem), Pribyslavice (Pribizl
2 CONC avensem), Dolni Kunice (Conowizensem), Godens (Godeninensem), Bzenec (Bisenzensem) and Budějovice (Budegewizensem). [6] In 1232, Constance founded Cloister Tichnowitz and retired to it as a nun. She died within the Cloister. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Issue===
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Vratislav of Bohemia (c. 1200 - before 1209).
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Judith of Bohemia (c. 1202 - 2 June 1230). Married -Bernhard von Spanheim, Duke of Carinthia
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Anna of Bohemia (c. 1204 - 23 June 1265). Married Henry II the Pious, Duke of Wrocław
