2 CONT Isabella of France (c. 1295 – August 22, 1358), known as the She-Wolf of France,[1] was the Queen consort of Edward II of England and mother of Edward III. She was the youngest surviving child and only surviving daughter of Philip
2 CONC  IV of France and Joan I of Navarre.
