2 CONT >The ''Flores historiarum'' of Bernard Guidonis names "''Robertum''" as youngest of the four sons of Philippe IV King of France, adding that he died "''in flore adolescentiæ suæ''" and was buried "''in monasterio sororem de Pyssia
2 CONC co''" in Aug 1308[869].  
