1 NOTE Called The Great.  Louis fought three wars with Venice (1342-46, 1357-58, 
2 CONT and 1378-81) for the control of the eastern Adriatic coast and was finally 
2 CONT successful. Bulgaria, Moldavia, Wallachia, and Serbia also acknowledged 
2 CONT his suzerainty, and when he succeeded his uncle, Casimir III, as king of 
2 CONT Poland, he became the most powerful ruler in eastern Europe. Louis 
2 CONT instituted many reforms in Hungary, which prospered during his reign. His 
2 CONT rule of Poland, where he made many concessions to the nobility, was less 
2 CONT beneficial.
