2 CONT 1.  Henry was King of England (1216-1272) who succeeded October 28, 1216, Gloucester Cathedral) his father, King John. A minor when he took thet hrone he did not take the reigns of Government himselfuntil 1234.  Hisre ign was marr
2 CONC ed by baronial opposition (the Barons Wars) led by Simonde Mo ntfort, whose representative parliament, called in 1265, isconsidered Eng land's first full parliament.  The Barons Wars wasdefeated after initi al success, thereafter 
2 CONC Henry ceeded much of hispower to his son, Edwa rd I, Longshanks, King of England.
2 CONT 2.  Burke say he was born 10 Oct 1206 and married 14 Jan, crowned 1216.
2 CONT
