2 NOTE Edward I "Longshanks" King Of England:
3 CONT
3 CONT Edward I (born 1239, ruled 1272-1307) was one of England's greatest kings. He was a handsome man, with fair hair and ruddy cheeks, and so tall that he was nicknamed Longshanks. He delighted in tournaments and hunting, but he was a
3 CONC lso practical and hardworking. For seven years before he came to the throne, he was the real ruler for his weak father, Henry III (see Henry, Kings of England; Montfort). He was in the Holy Land involved in the crusades when his f
3 CONC ather died, but there was no question that he would take the throne.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Edward I in his profile.
