1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John I, Count of Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from John I of Châtillon)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1254, John married Alix of Brittany (d. 1287), daughter of John I, Duke of Brittany and Blanche of Navarre. They had one child, Joanne. In 1256, he reunited Chartres with Blois on the death of his cousin Mathilde of Amboise. He
2 CONC  passed these lands on to Joanne before his death.
