1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Lava
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Beatrix of Brittany1,2
2 CONT *'''F, #18587, b. 1 December 1295, d. 9 December 1384
2 CONT *Father	Arthur II, Duke of Bretagne, Comte de Montfort b. 25 Jul 1262, d. 27 Aug 1312
2 CONT *Mother	Jolanda de Dreux b. 1263, d. 2 Aug 1322
2 CONT *'''     Beatrix of Brittany was born on 1 December 1295. She married Vidus (Guido) X, 4th Lord Laval''', son of Guido IX, 3rd Lord Laval, Sire de Vitre & d'Archy and Beatrix de Gavre, '''on 2 March 1315.2 Beatrix of Brittany died
2 CONC  on 9 December 1384 at age 89.2
2 CONT *'''Family     Vidus (Guido) X, 4th Lord Laval d. 18 Jun 1347
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **Vidus XII, 6th Lord Laval, Sire de Gavre & Chateaubriant, Seigneur de Belleville+ d. 21 Apr 1412
2 CONT **Beatrix de Laval+3 d. a Jan 1365
2 CONT **Guy XI de Laval, Sire de Laval, Vitre, & Gavre3 d. 22 Sep 1348
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S5598] Unknown author, Europaische Stammtafeln, by Isenburg, chart 137, 18 (Vol. 2).
2 CONT *[S11600] 40000 Ancestors of the Counts of Paris, 23-99.
2 CONT *[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. XIV, Tafel 137.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p619.htm#i18587 ______________________
2 CONT *The House of Laval is a family of barons, later counts, coming from the town of Laval, located in Northwestern France, part of the province of Maine before the French Revolution. The Laval were one of the most powerful families o
2 CONC f Maine during the Middle Ages and also had a presence in Brittany, where their prestige was similar to the one of the Rohan. The House of Laval played a significant role in Breton history and during the Hundred Years War and the 
2 CONC French Wars of Religion. They also favored the French Renaissance in Northwestern France, building several châteaux. The last male heir died during the 17th century, and his possessions went to the House of La Trémoille.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Barons of Laval
2 CONT *Guy V de Laval (d 1210) married Avoise de Craon and sired
2 CONT **Guy VI (d 1211) who died childless
2 CONT **Emma (c1200-1264, sister of Guy VI) married Mathieu II de Montmorency and gave birth to
2 CONT ***Guy VII (d 1267) who married Philippa de Vitre and sired
2 CONT ****Guy VIII (d 1295), who married Isabelle Beaumont and sired
2 CONT *****Guy IX (d 1333), who married Beatrix de Gavre and sired
2 CONT ******'''Guy X (d 1347), who married Beatrix of Brittany (daughter of Arthur II) and sired
2 CONT *******Guy XI (d 1348) and
2 CONT *******Guy XII (d 1412), who married Jeanne de Laval (a second cousin, descended from Guy VIII). His son Guy predeceased him in 1403. The title then passed to
2 CONT ********Anne (d 1466, daughter of Guy XII), who married Jean de Montfort, making him Guy XIII de Laval. They had several sons, including Guy XIV de Laval
2 CONT **Counts of Laval
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
