1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_of_Brabant,_Countess_of_Flanders
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret of Brabant ''' (9 February 1323 – 1380[1]) was Countess of Flanders by marriage. She was the second daughter of Duke John III of Brabant and Mary of Évreux. She was the only child of Duke John to have children. In 1347
2 CONC  she married Louis II of Flanders, who was then sixteen years old and already count of Flanders.[2] On 13 April 1350 their daughter, Margaret III, Countess of Flanders, was baptized.[3] Through this daughter, their only surviving 
2 CONC child, Brabant came under the influence of Burgundy when she married Philip the Bold. ..
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beatrix van Vlaanderen was the bastard child of Lodewijk II van Male, her mother is unknown. See her Source tab. Do NOT add her mother as Margaret of Brabant unless you have proof. MyHeritage user trees and FamilySearch.org use
2 CONC r trees are NOT historical sources.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG (''4 Apr 2023'') [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRABANT,%20LOUVAIN.htm#MargueriteBrabantdied1368 ''Brabant, Louvain'']
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Jean de Brabant''', son of JEAN II "der Friedfertige"...'''m ([19 Jul] 1311) Marie d'Evreux'''...[and he had 5 mistresses]. 
2 CONT >'''Jean III & his wife had six children:'''
2 CONT >'''1.''' '''Jeanne''' (24 Jun 1322-Brussels 1 Dec 1406, bur Brussels Carmelite Church).
2 CONT >'''2.''' '''Marguerite de Brabant''' (9 Feb 1323-1368, bur Lille Saint-Pierre).
2 CONT >The marriage contract between “''Edward...Roi d’Engleterre...nostre eisne filz Ducs de Cornewall''” and “''Johan Ducs de Lothringe, Brabantie et de Lemburgie et Markys de Seynt Empyre nostre...cousyn...damoisele Magaret file nost
2 CONC re dit cousyn''” is dated 3 May 1340[437]. 
2 CONT >King Edward III requested papal dispensation for the marriage between “''Johannem ducem Brabantiæ consanguineum nostrum...--- filiam dicti ducis Brabantiæ''” and “''Edwardum ducem Cornubiæ filium nostrum''” by charter dated 30 Oc
2 CONC t 1340[438].  
2 CONT >King Edward III requested papal dispensation for the marriage between “''Johannem ducem Brabantiæ consanguineum nostrum...filiam dicti ducis Brabantiæ''” and “''Rex...primogenitum nostrum Edwardum principem Walliæ et comitem Cest
2 CONC riæ''”, as well as the marriage between “''Johannem ducem Brabantiæ consanguineum nostrum...primogenitum dicti ducis''” and “''Rex...Isabellam filiam nostram''” by charter dated 26 Oct 1344[439].  
2 CONT >The ''Oude Kronik van Brabant'' names "''Johannam, Margaretam comitissam Flandrie, et Mariam coniugem Reynaldi Grossi ducis Ghelrie secundi''" as the three daughters of "''Johannes tertius''" and his wife "''Mariam filiam Ludowic
2 CONC i comitis Eboracensis''"[440].  
2 CONT >The marriage contract must have been terminated before Nov 1345 when negotiations started for Prince Edward’s marriage to one of the daughters of the king of Portugal[441]. 
2 CONT >'''Betrothed''' ([1340], contract terminated before Nov 1345) to '''Edward of England "of Woodstock"''' Duke of Cornwall, son of EDWARD III King of England & his wife Philippa de Hainaut (Woodstock Palace, Oxfordshire 15 Jun 1330
2 CONC -Palace of Westminster 8 Jun 1376, bur Canterbury Cathedral, Kent).  
2 CONT >'''m''' (Saint-Quentin 6 Jun 1347) '''Louis II “de Mâle”''' Count of Flanders, son of '''Louis I Count of Flanders''' & his wife '''Marguerite de France Ctss d'Artois''' (Maldeghem/Mâle, near Bruges 25 Nov 1330-Saint-Omer 30 Jan 
2 CONC 1383, bur Lille Saint-Pierre).
2 CONT >'''3. Marie''' (1325-1 Mar 1399, bur Brussels)....
2 CONT >'''4. Jean''' (24 Nov 1327-[1335/36], bur Tervueren)....
2 CONT >'''5. Henri''' (-29 Nov 1349, bur Tervueren)....
2 CONT >'''6. Godefroi''' (-after 3 Feb 1352, bur Tervueren)....
2 CONT >—————————————————
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis-II-van-Vlaanderen-Comte-de-Flandres-Flanders/6000000185363088822 LOUIS de Flandre], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis-II-Dampierre-comte-de-Nevers-de-Flandre-et-de-Rethel/6000000001500850
2 CONC 848?through=6000000185363088822 LOUIS I] Count of Flanders & his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Marguerite-de-Flandre-Princesse-de-France-comtesse-de-Bourgogne-de-Nevers/6000000001096256553?through=6000000185363088822 Marguerit
2 CONC e de France] Ctss d'Artois (Maldeghem/Mâle, near Bruges 25 Nov 1330-Saint-Omer 30 Jan 1383, bur Lille Saint-Pierre).
2 CONT The Iohannis de Thilrode Chronicon names "Ludovicus…filius fuit Ludovicus dictus de Male"[810].  He succeeded his father in 1346 as LOUIS II “de Male” Count of Flanders, Comte de Nevers et de Rethel, Comte Palatin de Bourgogne, Co
2 CONC mte d'Artois.  After his brother-in-law Wenzel I Comte de Luxembourg, Duke of Brabant, initiated negotiations with his brother concerning the latter's eventual inheritance of the childless Wenzel's properties, Count Louis occupied
2 CONC  Mechelen and Duke Wenzel was forced to flee to Limburg.  The dispute was settled by the peace of Ath under which Mechelen and Antwerp were transferred to Flanders, and Count Louis was granted the right to bear the title Duke of B
2 CONC rabant[811].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (Papal dispensation Avignon 14 Mar 1335) to his first cousin, YOLANDE de Flandre, dame de Cassel, daughter of ROBERT de Flandre, Comte de Marle, Seigneur de Cassel & his wife Jeanne de Bretagne, dame de Nogent-le-Rotrou 
2 CONC (château d'Alluyes, Eure-et-Loir 2 Feb or 15 Sep 1326 or 1331-château de Nieppe dit de La Motte-au-Bois, Hazebrouck, Nord 12 Dec 1395, bur Bar-le-Duc, église collégiale Saint-Maxe). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (before 1347, renewed 13 Mar 1347, terminated before 6 Jun 1347) to ISABELLA of England, daughter of EDWARD III King of England & his wife Philippa de Hainaut (Woodstock Palace, Oxfordshire 16 Feb or [Mar] or 16 Jun [133
2 CONC 2 or 1334]-[15 Mar/4 May] 1379 or [17 Jun/5 Oct] 1382, bur Greyfriars Church, Newgate, London).  A charter dated 13 Mar 1346 (O.S.) records the renewal of the contract for the marriage between “Loys contes de Flandres, de Nevers e
2 CONC t de Rechest” and “Edward...Roi d´Engleterre...Ysabel ainsnee fille”[812]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Saint-Quentin 6 Jun 1347) [https://www.geni.com/people/Margaretha-de-M%C3%A2le-Flanders-Nevers/6000000001504983220?through=6000000185363088822 '''MARGUERITE de Brabant'''], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-III-Duke
2 CONC -of-Brabant/5566580638230026755?through=6000000000498433774 JEAN III Duke of Brabant] & his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Marie-d-Evreux/6000000000498433774?through=6000000001504983220 Marie d'Evreux] (9 Feb 1323-1368, bur Lil
2 CONC le Saint-Pierre).  The Oude Kronik van Brabant names "Johannam, Margaretam comitissam Flandrie, et Mariam coniugem Reynaldi Grossi ducis Ghelrie secundi" as the three daughters of "Johannes tertius" and his wife "Mariam filiam Lud
2 CONC owici comitis Eboracensis"[813]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-III-Countess-of-Flanders/6000000004532537004?through=6000000001504983220 MARGUERITE de Flandre] (Mâle near Bruges 1350, chr 13 Apr 1350-Arras 16 Mar 1405, bur Lille, église Saint-P
2 CONC ierre).  The marriage contract between “Philippes Duc de Bourgongne” and “Marguerite de Flandres” is dated 21 Mar 1356 (O.S.)[814].  The Iohannis de Thilrode Chronicon records the marriage of "filiam comitis nostri Ludovici de Mal
2 CONC e Margaretam" and "Philippus filius regis Francie"[815].  A charter dated 20 Jul 1364 records negotiations for the marriage between “nostre...cousin le conte de Flandres...Margarete duchesse de Burgoigne file au dit conte” and “no
2 CONC stre...filz Esmon de Langele”[816].  The contract for the marriage between “Edward...roi Engleterre...messieur Esmon counte de Cantebrigg filz au dit roi” and “Loys counte de Flandres, duc de Brabant, counte de Nyvers et de Reches
2 CONC t et sire de Malynes...dame Margarete duchesse de Burgoigne sa fille”[817].  The Chronicon Angliæ records the betrothal of “Edmundus de Langley filius regis Edwardi” and “filiam et heredem...comitis Flandriæ”, adding that “rex Fra
2 CONC nciæ Karolus” blocked the marriage, dated to 1364 from the context[818].  She succeeded her father in 1383 as MARGUERITE III Ctss of Flanders, Ctss d'Artois, Ctss de Nevers and Rethel, Ctss Palatine of Burgundy.  Dss of Brabant an
2 CONC d Limburg, Markgravine of Antwerp, Dame de Malines 1404.  m firstly (Papal dispensation 31 Jan 1356, contract Paris 21 Mar 1357, Arras, église Saint-Vaast 14 May 1357, not consummated) PHILIPPE I "de Rouvres" Duke of Burgundy, son
2 CONC  of PHILIPPE "Monsieur" de Bourgogne [Capet], Comte d'Artois, Comte Palatin de Bourgogne, Comte d'Auvergne et de Boulogne & Jeanne I Ctss d'Auvergne et de Boulogne (château de Rouvres, Côte d'Or end Aug 1346-château de Rouvres 21 
2 CONC Nov 1361, bur Abbaye de Cîteaux).  Betrothed (19 Oct 1364) to EDMUND of Langley, son of EDWARD III King of England & his wife Philippa de Hainaut (Abbot’s Langley, Hertfordshire 5 Jun 1341-King’s Langley, Hertfordshire 1 Aug 1402,
2 CONC  bur King’s Langley, Church of the Dominican Friars).  This betrothal was arranged under the Treaty of Dover 19 Oct 1364, but the French persuaded Pope Urban V to refuse a dispensation on grounds of consanguinity[819].  m secondly
2 CONC  (by proxy 12 Apr 1369, in person Gent 19 Jun 1369) PHILIPPE II "le Hardi" Duke of Burgundy, son of JEAN II "le Bon" King of France & his first wife Bonne de Luxembourg (Pontoise 15 Jan 1342-Hall 27 Apr 1404, bur Dijon). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II had eleven illegitimate children by various mistresses (the order of their births is uncertain):
