1 OCCU Countess of Vendôme and of Castres (1372-1403), Countess of Maison and Montoire
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catherine_of_Vend%C3%B4me
2 CONT
2 CONT and in French:  http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catherine_de_Vend%C3%B4me
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine de Vendôme (d. 1412), countess of Vendôme and of Castres (1372-1403) was a French noblewoman of the House of Montoire. She was the daughter of John VI of Vendôme and Jeanne of Ponthieu.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1364 she married John I, Count of La Marche[2] and they had:
2 CONT
2 CONT James II, Count of La Marche and Castres (1370–1438) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (b. 1373), a nun at Poissy 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, Count of Vendôme (1376–1446) 
2 CONT
2 CONT John, Lord of Carency (1378–1457), married c. 1416 Catherine, daughter of Philip of Artois, Count of Eu, without issue, married in 1420 at Le Mans, his mistress Jeanne de Vendômois, with whom he had issue 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne (c. 1380 – September 1408, Paris), married in 1401 John of Berry, Count of Montpensier (d. 1401), married in Paris in 1402 Louis VII, Duke of Bavaria 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (1386 – aft. 11 September 1463), Lady of Brehencourt, married Jean de Baynes, Lord of Croix 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte (1388 – 15 January 1422), married in 1411 at Nicosia King Janus of Cyprus 
2 CONT
2 CONT She inherited Vendôme on the death of her niece Jeanne and administered it jointly with her husband then (after his death) with her second son Louis until 1403.
