2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00004914&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite de Foix, (c. 1453 [1] – 15 May 1486, Nantes), was, by marriage, Duchess of Brittany from 1474 to 1486.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Gaston IV of Foix (1425-1472), Count of Foix, and Eleanor of Navarre (1425-1479).
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 June 1474, at Clisson, she married Francis II, Duke of Brittany (1435-1488), son of Richard of Brittany (1395-1438), comte d'Étampes (1421-1438), and of Marguerite d'Orléans (1406-1466), comtesse de Vertus (b. 1423). It was 
2 CONC François' second marriage, his first wife (Marguerite of Brittany) having died in 1469.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the union were born two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne (1477-1514), Duchess of Brittany (1488-1514), and Queen of France from 1491 to 1498 and again from 1499 to 1514, being the wife in succession to Charles VIII and Louis XII
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabeau (1478-1490)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite de Foix is buried in the cathedral of Nantes, beside her husband and Marguerite of Brittany, in a magnificant tomb named the Tomb of François II, and which is a chief French work of the Renaissance.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Margaret of Foix at Genealogics
