1 OCCU Roi de Naples de Sicile et de Jâerusalem, King of Naples, Duke of Anjou, roi de SICILE (1384 - 1417), duc d´Anjou (1384 - 1417) comte du Maine et de Provence (1384 -1417) etc. Gouverneur de la Ville de Paris (1413), Comte du Maine
2 CONC  Sep 21 1384
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_II_of_Anjou
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II of Anjou (1377–April 29, 1417), was the rival of [https://www.geni.com/people/N%C3%A1polyi-L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3/6000000002176658451  Ladislas] as King of Naples. He was a member of the House of Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Toulouse, Louis II was the son of Louis I of Anjou, King of Naples, and came into his Angevin inheritance, which included Provence, in 1384, with his rival Charles of Durazzo (father of Ladislas), of the senior Angevin lin
2 CONC e, in possession of Naples.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1386, the underage Ladislas was expelled soon after his father died. Louis II was crowned King of Naples by the Avignonese antipope Clement VII on November 1, 1389 and took possession of Naples the following year. He was ousted
2 CONC  in turn by his rival in 1399.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1409, Louis liberated Rome from Ladislas' occupation; in 1410, as an ally of the antipope John XXIII he attacked Ladislas and defeated him at Roccasecca (1411). Eventually Louis lost his Neapolitan support and had to retire. Hi
2 CONC s claim to Naples passed to his son, Louis III.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Yolande of Aragon (1384–1443) in Arles in 1400, giving him a possibility of inheriting the throne of Aragon through her right. Her father, King John I of Aragon had died in 1396, and her uncle king Martin I of Aragon di
2 CONC ed in 1410.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II died at his chateau of Angers, the heart of Anjou; he is buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis and Yolande had five surviving children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Louis III of Anjou, titular King of Naples, Duke of Anjou, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT *René of Anjou, King of Naples, Duke of Anjou, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Charles of Le Maine (1414–1472), Count of Maine
2 CONT
2 CONT *Marie of Anjou (1404 – 1463), married 1422, Bourges Charles VII of France
2 CONT
2 CONT *Yolande (1412, Arles – 1440), married 1431, Nantes Francis I, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Louis II, Duc d'Anjou1 M, #113405, b. 5 October 1377, d. 26 April 1417
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II, Duc d'Anjou|b. 5 Oct 1377\nd. 26 Apr 1417|p11341.htm#i113405|Louis I, Duc d'Anjou|b. 23 Jul 1339\nd. 20 Sep 1384|p10522.htm#i105214|Marie de Châtillon|b. c 1343\nd. 12 Nov 1404|p11364.htm#i113635|Jean I., Roi de France|b
2 CONC . 26 Apr 1319\nd. 8 Apr 1364|p10314.htm#i103138|Bonne J. de Luxembourg|b. 20 May 1315\nd. 11 Sep 1349|p10316.htm#i103159|Charles de Châtillon, Comte de Blois|d. 29 Sep 1364|p11364.htm#i113636|Jeanne de Penthièvre|b. c 1319\nd. 10 
2 CONC Oct 1384|p353.htm#i3527|
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=8 Mar 2007 Consanguinity Index=0.3%
2 CONT      Louis II, Duc d'Anjou was born on 5 October 1377. He was the son of Louis I, Duc d'Anjou and Marie de Châtillon.2 He married Yolande de Aragón, daughter of Juan I, Rey de Aragón and Mathe d'Armagnac, on 2 December 1400. He di
2 CONC ed on 26 April 1417 at age 39.
2 CONT      Louis II, Duc d'Anjou was a member of the House of Valois.3 He gained the title of King Louis II of Naples.1 He succeeded to the title of Comte de Provence in 1384.3 He gained the title of Duc d'Anjou in 1384. Children of Lou
2 CONC is II, Duc d'Anjou and Yolande de Aragón 1.Charles le Maine+4 2.Louis III, Duc d'Anjou3 b. 1403, d. 1434 3.Maria d'Anjou+2 b. 1404, d. 1463 4.René I 'the Good', Duc d'Anjou+2 b. 16 Jan 1408, d. 10 Jul 1480 Citations 1.[S16] Jirí L
2 CONC ouda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 46. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession. 2.[S16] Louda and MacLagan,
2 CONC  Lines of Succession, table 65. 3.[S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 87. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World
2 CONC . 4.[S130] Wikipedia, online http;//www.wikipedia.org. Hereinafter cited as Wikipedia.
