1 NOTE Duke of the House of Anjou.
2 CONT Duke of Naples.
2 CONT Duke of Sicily.
1 NOTE DUKE OF BAR 1430; DUKE OF ANJOU, ANDEGAVIA LORRAINE (1431), BARRENSIS, &
2 CONT CALABRIA; G.M. PRIEURE DE SION FROM 1418; EARL OF PROVENCE, CENNOMANIA, &
2 CONT GUISE; KING OF SICILY & ARAGON; ALSO LISTED AS "REYNAR"; KNOWN AS "THE GOOD"
1 NOTE Duke of Anjou, Count of Provence and Piedmont. Failed in his efforts (1438 to 1442) to make good his claim to be King of Naples. Ultimately devoted himself to Provencal poetry and agriculture at Aix-en-Provence. After his death, P
2 CONC rovence was united with the French crown. {Chamber�s Biographical Dictionary} [GADD.GED]
1 NOTE Il hâerite du royaume de Naples áa la mort de Jeanne II en 1435. Il n'arrive cependant pas áa le reconquâerir sur Alphonse V d'Aragon (entre 1438 et 1442).
2 CONT
2 CONT Il apporte son soutien áa Charles VII, roi de France, contre les Anglais.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il centralise l'administration, crâee de nouveaux impãots, protáege le commerce. Mâecáene et poáete, il entretient une vie artistique et littâeraire active dans ses diverses possessions et passe áa la postâeritâe sous le nom de "B
2 CONC on Roi Renâe".
2 CONT
2 CONT Il láegue la Provence áa son neveu, Charles du Maine, qui meurt sans enfants. Louis XI pourra alors râeunir la Provence áa la France
