1 NOTE {geni:about_me} COAT OF ARMS FOLCH DE CORDONA:  The ducal coat of arms of the Segorbe dukes, a group of the "Aragon" family names, grafted to the "Folch de Cardona" family, who had their own much simpler ducal coat of arms, marrie
2 CONC d since 1516, but keeping both family names depending on circumstances, group of influence, administrated lands, etc. Since the middle of the 16th century a line of the "Fernandez de Cordoba" families was grafted, too. The uses of
2 CONC  the family names, "Aragon", "Folch de Cardona" and "Fernandez de Cordoba" could depend on personal circumstances, wealth and lands, etc. By the beginnings of the 18th century, they became intertwined with the dukes of Medinaceli 
2 CONC who started to use "Fernandez de Cordoba", as the original "de la Cerda" ducal family ended their complicated family saga becoming political prisoners of the new Bourbon Royal Family, dying while in prison at Pamplona, Spain, in 1
2 CONC 711. The actual duchess, holding a surprising number of all kinds of titles, several of them dukedoms, is a "Fernandez de Cordoba".
2 CONT
2 CONT D. Beringeira de Cardona filha de D. Romão Folche de Cardona Conde D. Pedro fl 141 N 10
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 D. Gonçalo de Aguiar
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 João Gonçalves de Macedo segundo alguns no § 1 N 6
2 CONT
2 CONT (NFP, Gayo, MACEDOS § 6 N 5).
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Los castillos de Malda y Maldanell (Amaldino y Amaldinella) fueron vendidos por Guillem de Cardona a su hija doña Berenguel en 1266.
2 CONT
2 CONT " El trovador Gonçal'Eanes Dovinhal: estudio histórico y edición" de Antonia Víñez Sánchez - Pág.76
