1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Vescomte de Canet
2 CONT * Senyor de la Guàrdia
2 CONT
2 CONT El vizcondado de Canet fue un Título nobiliario con jurisdicción concedido por Sancho I de Mallorca, en 1321, a favor de don Guillem de Guardia (o Saguàrdia) y de Canet, consejero real y señor de los castillos de Guàrdia y de la b
2 CONC aronía de Canet.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://heraldicacatalana.blogspot.com.uy/2011/03/armas-de-los-titulos-catalanes-xxxvii.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Great Catalan encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillem de Saguàrdia and de Canet William III of Canet
2 CONT
2 CONT History
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Ponç de Saguàrdia and Saportella , and of Timbor, daughter and heiress of William II of Canet, he served King Sancho I of Mallorca, who sent him as ambassador to James II of Aragon as he prepared to conquer the 'island of S
2 CONC ardinia (1321). ?, ? - ?, 1324 He was the favorite adviser to the sovereign, who erected his lordships in the viscounty of Canet in 1321 and appointed him as tutor to his nephew, the future Jaume III of Mallorca. But he died a few
2 CONC  months before his sovereign.
