1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_of_Brienne
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MAINE.htm#LouisBriennedied1297A<br/>
2 CONT LOUIS de Brienne "d'Acre", son of JEAN de Brienne King of Jerusalem & his third wife Infanta doña Berenguela de Castilla y León (-14 Sep after 1285, after 1 Sep 1297).  The Chronique de Guillaume de Nangis records in 1244 that Jea
2 CONC n Emperor of Constantinople sent "ses trois fils, Alphonse, Jean et Louis, encore enfants" to Louis IX King of France[426].  He succeeded as Vicomte de Beaumont, de iure uxoris.  “Louis fils de Jean roi de Jérusalem et Agnès sa fe
2 CONC mme” granted privileges to the monks of Vivoin by charter dated 1253[427].  “Louis vicomte de Beaumont fils du roi de Jérusalem et Agnès vicomtesse héréditaire de Beaumont sa femme” settled various disputed matters with the monks 
2 CONC of Vivoin by charter dated Feb 1254 (N.S.)[428].  “Louis vicomte de Beaumont, et Agnès sa femme” donated revenue from Lude to Etival by charter dated 1285[429].  The necrology of Etival records the death 14 Sep of “Louis vicomte d
2 CONC e Beaumont” and his burial at Etival[430].  One table in Europäische Stammtafeln records Louis’s death “after Sep 1297”, another “1285”[431].  The primary source which confirms the former date has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1253 or before) AGNES de Beaumont, daughter of --- de Beaumont-au-Maine & his wife --- ([1236/38] or before-[9 May 1301 or 28 Nov after 1304], bur Etival). ... ... ... ... ...
2 CONT
2 CONT   Louis & his wife had seven children: 
