2 CONT BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis was the son of Jean de Brienne, king of Jerusalem and Latin emperor of Constantinople, and Berenguela of León and Castile. On 12 February 1253 Louis married Agnès de Beaumont, daughter and heiress of Raoul VIII de Beaumont. 
2 CONC They had eight children of whom two sons and two daughters would have progeny. In 1253 Louis and Agnès allowed the nuns of Vivoin to expand the court of their monastery. In 1255 Louis was present at the court of his first cousin, 
2 CONC Alfonso X, king of Castile and León. Louis died after 1 September 1297 and his widow on 28 November after 1304. Louis was buried in the chartreuse du Parc-d'Orques, where his father also lies buried. His wife was buried in the abb
2 CONC aye d'Etival.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 	1. [S00301]   ~Europäische Stammtafeln, J.A. Stargardt Verlag, Marburg, Schwennicke, Detlev (Ed.), Reference: III 683
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Louis de Brienne was the son of Jean I de Brienne, Emperor of Constantinople and Berengaria de Castilla.1 He married Agnes, Vicomtesse de Beaumont, daughter of Raoul VIII, Vicomte de Beaumont and Agnes (?), on 12 February 1253.2 H
2 CONC e died after 1263.3
2 CONT      Louis de Brienne was also known as Louis d'Acre.1 As a result of his marriage, Louis de Brienne was styled as Vicomte de Beaumont, jure uxoris.1 Children of Louis de Brienne and Agnes, Vicomtesse de Beaumont
2 CONT
