1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===== Attention homonymy with https://geni.com/people/Ramon-Berenguer-IV-the-Saint-count-of-Barcelona/6000000010463529059 (1113-1162)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramon_Berenguer_IV,_Count_of_Provence ''[23 languages]''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ramon Berenguer V''' (French: ''Raimond-Bérenger''; 1198 – 19 August 1245) was a member of the House of Barcelona who ruled as count of Provence and Forcalquier. He was the first count of Provence to live in the county in more 
2 CONC than one hundred years. During the minority of a previous count, the regency was exercised by Ramon Berenguer IV de Barcelona, who is sometimes counted among the counts of Provence. .. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/PROVENCE.htm#RaymondBerengerIVdied1245
2 CONT
2 CONT '''RAYMOND BERENGER de Provence''', son of ALPHONSE II Comte de Provence [Aragon-Barcelona] & his wife Gersende de Sabran Ctss de Forcalquier ([1198]-Aix 19 Aug 1245, bur Aix-en-Provence, église de Saint Jean de Jérusalem).  “Gars
2 CONC endis uxor quondam Ildefonsi comitis Provinciæ” donated her rights “in comitatu Forcalqueriensi”, granted by “Guillelmo quondam comite Forcalqueriensi avo meo”, to “Raymundo Berengario filio meo” with “filiæ meæ sororis tuæ Garsen
2 CONC dis” as substitute should he die, with the consent of “patre meo Raines de Castelar”, by charter dated 30 Nov 1209[422].  He succeeded his father in 1209 as RAYMOND BERENGER IV Comte de Provence et de Forcalquier.  Under his testa
2 CONC ment dated 20 Jun 1238, he designated his fourth daughter as his heir[423].  The testament of “R. Berengarius…comes et marchio Provincie et comes Forcalquerii”, dated 20 Jun 1238, names “Margaritam filiam nostrum…reginam Francie…E
2 CONC lionors filiam nostrum…reginam Anglie…Sanciam filiam nostram” and appoints “Beatricem filiam nostrum heredem generalem”[424].  The Annales Sancti Victoris Massilienses record the death "1245 XIV Kal Sep" of "Raimundus Berengarius 
2 CONC comes Provincie" at Aix[425].  The Obituaire of Forcalquier St Mary records the death "XIV Kal Sep" of "Raymundus Berengarii…comes Provincie et Forcalquerii"[426].  The Thalamus de Montpellier records the death Aug 1244 of "R. Ber
2 CONC enguier coms de Proensa" at Aix[427]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (Betrothed 5 Jun 1219, Dec 1220) BEATRIX de Savoie, daughter of THOMAS I Comte de Savoie & his wife Marguerite [Beatrix] de Genève ([1205][428]-Dec 1266 or 4 Jan 1267). .. ... .... 
2 CONT
2 CONT    Comte Raymond Bérenger IV & his wife had five children:
2 CONT #           MARGUERITE de Provence (St Maime near Forcalquier Spring 1221-Paris, Abbaye de St Marcel 21 Dec 1295, bur église de l'Abbaye royale de Saint-Denis). .. ...<br> ''m'' (Cathedral of St Etienne, Sens, Yonne 27 May 1234) L
2 CONC OUIS IX King of France, .. 
2 CONT #   ELEONORE de Provence (Aix-en-Provence [1223]-Amesbury Abbey, Wiltshire 24/25 Jun 1291, bur Amesbury Abbey). <br> ''m'' (Betrothed 22 Jun 1235, Canterbury 14 Jan 1236) HENRY III King of England, ..
2 CONT # SANCHA de Provence (Aix-en-Provence [1225]-Berkhamstead Castle, Buckinghamshire 5 or 9 Nov 1261, bur Hayles Abbey, Gloucestershire). <br> ''Betrothed'' (contract before Jun 1240, ''annulled'' Jun 1240) to GUIGUES Dauphin de Vien
2 CONC nois Comte d'Albon ..  <br>''Betrothed'' (Aug 1241) to RAYMOND VII Comte de Toulouse, .. <br> ''m'' (Contract 17 Jul 1242, Westminster 22 Nov 1243) as his second wife, RICHARD Earl of Cornwall, son of JOHN King of England ..
2 CONT #     RAYMOND de Provence (-young). 
2 CONT #  BEATRICE de Provence ([1232/34]-Naples 23 Sep 1267, bur Naples, Cathedral of San Gennaro, transferred 1277 to Aix-en-Provence, Church of St Jean de Jerusalem). .. ... .... <br> ''m'' (Aix-en-Provence 31 Jan 1246) as his first w
2 CONC ife, CHARLES de France Comte d'Anjou et de Maine, .. CHARLES I King of Sicily ..
2 CONT
