1 NOTE Berenger was the last and most illustrious of the Royal ProvenÃal Counts;and,
2 CONT even had he not been the sovereign of the land of song, his own verseswould
2 CONT have entitled him to a distinguised rank among the Troubadour poets.
2 CONT He was relatively impoverished count who could provide little dowry forhis four
2 CONT daughters, who despite that became the Queen of England, Queen of France,Queen of the Germans and Queen of Naples and Sicily.
