2 CONT [edit] Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT [show]Ancestors of Louis VIII of France
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 May 1200, at the age of twelve, Louis married Blanche of Castile (4 March 1188 – 26 November 1252).
2 CONT  1.Blanche (1205–1206).
2 CONT  2.Agnes (b. and d. 1207).
2 CONT  3.Philip (9 September 1209 – July 1218), married (or only betrothed) in 1217 to Agnes of Donzy.
2 CONT  4.Alphonse (b. and d. Lorrez-le-Bocage, 23 January 1213).
2 CONT  5.John (b. and d. Lorrez-le-Bocage, 23 January 1213), twin of Alphonse.
2 CONT  6.Louis IX (Poissy, 25 April 1214 – 25 August 1270, Tunis), King of France as successor to his father.
2 CONT  7.Robert (25 September 1216 – 9 February 1250, killed in Battle of Al Mansurah, Egypt)
2 CONT  8.Philip (2 January 1218–1220).
2 CONT  9.John Tristan (21 July 1219–1232), Count of Anjou and Maine.
2 CONT  10.Alphonse (Poissy, 11 November 1220 – 21 August 1271, Corneto), Count of Poitou and Auvergne, and by marriage, of Toulouse.
2 CONT  11.Philip Dagobert (20 February 1222–1232).
2 CONT  12.Isabelle (14 April 1225 – 23 February 1269).
2 CONT  13.Charles Etienne (21 March 1226 – 7 January 1285), Count of Anjou and Maine, by marriage Count of Provence and Forcalquier, and King of Sicily.
