2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche of Castile was born in 1188 in Palencia, Spain and died in 1252 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche married King Louis VIII "Le Lion" of France. King Louis was born in 1187. He was the son of King Philip II of France. He died in 1226 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche - When Louis died he made Blanche Regent and guardian of their children. Louis Ix was then 12 and Blanche ruled France alone from 1226 to 1234; dealing successfully both with a coalition of the powerful barons in 1226 - sh
2 CONC  e rode into battle, dressed in white on a white horse, at the head of her troops - and with the attacks of Henry III in 1230; she was less successful with the student disturbances in Paris, which caused the university to leave th
2 CONC e  city from 1229 to 1233. She made clever alliances and expanded her territory, gaining Blois, Chartres and Sancerre by agreement with her ally Thibaut of Champagne, and Toulouse and Provence through skilful marriage treaties. A 
2 CONC fo rceful character, she retained a powerful influence over Louis IX ('Saint Louis') after he came to the throne in 1236, with regard to both state affairs and religion. Her second regency lasted from 1248, when Louis set out (aga
2 CONC ins t her will) on a crusade, until her death four years later. With her third son, Alphonse, she maintained peace at home, despite the depletion of the country necessary to support the extravagant crusade, and negotiated personal
2 CONC ly f or Louis' release after the battle of El Mansurah.
2 CONT
