2 CONT [edit] Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche (1205–1206). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes (b. and d. 1207). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe (9 September 1209 – July 1218), married (or only betrothed) in 1217 to Agnes of Donzy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alphonse (b. and d. Lorrez-le-Bocage, 23 January 1213). 
2 CONT
2 CONT John (b. and d. Lorrez-le-Bocage, 23 January 1213), twin of Alphonse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis IX (Poissy, 25 April 1214 – 25 August 1270, Tunis), King of France as successor to his father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert (25 September 1216 – 9 February 1250, killed in battle, Manssurah, Egypt) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe (2 January 1218–1220). 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tristan (21 July 1219–1232), Count of Anjou and Maine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alphonse (Poissy, 11 November 1220 – 21 August 1271, Corneto), Count of Poitou and Auvergne, and by marriage, of Toulouse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe Dagobert (20 February 1222–1232). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel (14 April 1225 – 23 February 1269). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Etienne (21 March 1226 – 7 January 1285), Count of Anjou and Maine, by marriage Count of Provence and Folcalquier, and King of Sicily. 
