1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maria of Aragon, Queen of Castile
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria of Aragon (Spanish:María de Aragón) (1396 – 1445) was the first wife and Queen consort of John II of Castile. The daughter of Ferdinand I of Aragon and Eleanor of Alburquerque, she married her cousin John in 1418. They had f
2 CONC our children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalina (1422-1424)
2 CONT
2 CONT Leonor (1423-1425)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry IV of Castile (1425-1474)
2 CONT
2 CONT María (1428-1429)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Maria of Aragon; (1396 – 1445) was the first wife and Queen consort of John II of Castile. The daughter of Ferdinand I of Aragon and Eleanor of Alburquerque, she married her cousin John in 1418. They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalina (1422-1424) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Leonor (1423-1425) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry IV of Castile (1425-1474) 
2 CONT
2 CONT María (1428-1429) 
2 CONT
2 CONT After her death in 1445 her husband married Infanta Isabel of Portugal and they became the parents of Isabella I of Castile.
