1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jofre de Rocabertí i de Serrallonga (? -?,? - 1342) known as Jofre V was Viscount of Rocabertí between 1324 and 1342 . [1] He married Elisenda de Montcada, [1] niece of the queen of the same name and daughter of the royal butler O
2 CONC t de Montcada , with whom he had three children: Felip Dalmau I de Rocabertí , heir to the viscounty, Benet and Joan Guerau .
2 CONT
2 CONT He began his government with problems in the barony of Maçanet de Cabrenys due to problems of vassalage with the king of Mallorca , but as this barony passed to his brother Guillem Galceran de Rocabertí this conflict did not affec
2 CONC t him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a reputation as a good diplomat and this made him one of the five nobles who were to settle the succession to the kingdom of Mallorca after the death of Sanç I of Mallorca , along with the Viscount of Cardona , Bernat de Ca
2 CONC brera , the Count of Pallars and Guillem de Montcada . [1] He was also in charge of mediating between the count of Pallars and the viscount of Cardona, although the intervention of the infant Alfonso in favor of the first, who was
2 CONC  his brother-in-law, thwarted the action.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended the solemn coronation of this child ( Alfonso III the Benign ), [1] in Zaragoza ( 1328 ) and that Ramon Muntaner explains with great profusion of details in his work. He was also present at the coronation of Peter III 
2 CONC the Ceremonious in the same city ( 1336 ). He took part in the Granada campaign in 1331 , which proved a failure. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________
2 CONT
