2 CONT Philippa d'Avesnes of Hainault
2 CONT Memorial
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jun. 24, 1311 Valenciennes Departement du Nord Nord-Pas-de-Calais, France Death: 	Aug. 14, 1369 Windsor Windsor and Maidenhead Royal Borough Berkshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT English Monarch. Queen consort of King Edward III. The daughter of William III "The Good", Count of Hainault and Jean de Valois, she married Edward on January 24, 1328. She often accompanied him on this foreign travels, and Edward
2 CONC  was devoted to her. The couple had 13 children, including 5 sons whose rivalry would later set into motion the Wars of the Roses. She was said to be tender-hearted, and interfered little in politics. (bio by: Kristen Conrad) 
2 CONT
