1 NAME Béatrice "Contessone" /des Baux di Avellino/
2 GIVN Béatrice "Contessone"
2 SURN des Baux di Avellino
2 NICK Béatrix
2 NICK dite Contessona
2 NICK de Baux
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#BeatrixBauxdied1344
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Bertrand des/de Baux, Conte di Avellino, and his second wife Agathe de Mévouillon
2 CONT
2 CONT BEATRIX de Baux “Contessone” (-[1324/14 Apr 1328]).  Her family origin and marriage are indicated by the following document: "Alasacie de Lambesc abbesse de Saint-Césaire d’Arles" accepted the homage of “Jean dauphin de Viennois” 
2 CONC for “les châteaux de Vinsobres, Mirabel et Nyons”, reserving rights assigned “en dot à Béatrix d’Avellin épouse de noble Guy dauphin seigneur de Montauban frère de Jean”, by charter dated 7 Aug 1309[489].  A charter dated 31 Jan 1
2 CONC 317 records an agreement between "Jean II dauphin-viennois" and “Béatrix de Baux d’Avellin sa belle-sœur, veuve de Guy de Montauban” concerning her dower[490].  The testament of "Béatrix d’Avellin veuve de Guy baron de Montauban",
2 CONC  dated 1324, bequeathed property to “sa fille Anne de Viennois princesse d’Orange...sa sœur Sibylle épouse d’Aymar IV Comte de Valentinois”[491].  She died before 11 Apr 1328, the date of the charter which names her daughter.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m GUIGUES de Viennois Seigneur de Montauban, son of HUMBERT de la Tour du Pin et de Coligny, Dauphin de Viennois & his wife Anne Dauphine de Viennois [Bourgogne-Capet] (-Pont-de-Sorgues-en-Provence [23/31] Jan 1317, bur Saint-Andr
2 CONC é de Grenoble). 
