1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   Comte Aymar [V] & his second wife had thirteen children: 
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provvaldi.htm#LouisPoitiersdied1345
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.      '''   LOUIS de Poitiers ''' (-killed in battle Auberoche 21 or 23 Oct 1345, bur Crest Franciscan monastery).  His parentage is confirmed by a charter dated May 1329 which records that "Ademarus comes et Ademarus eius filiu
2 CONC s", with the consent of "Sibilia de Baucio uxore dicti Ademari iunioris et Ludovico de Pictavia milite dictorum coniugium filio", donated "castra sua Pivacii, Boloniæ, Barrii et S. Vincentii de Barro, Vivariensis diocesis" to "Gui
2 CONC chardo [de Pictavia filii dicti Ademari iunioris]…in minori ætate"[1415].  The testament of "Aimard de Poitiers Comte de Valentinois", dated 13 Jan 1332 (presumably O.S.), appoints "Loys son filz aisné" as his heir, with "Aimaret 
2 CONC son petit filz…Othe…Aimaret, Guillaume et Henry ses autres filz…Charles son fils dernier né…Amedé son frere ou Aimaret son fils ou autres de ses enfans…les enfans de sa fille Alienor mariée à Bernard de la Voute"[1416].  The testa
2 CONC ment of "dominus Aimarus de Pictavia Comes Valentinensis et Diensis", dated 12 Aug 1339, appoints "filium suum primogenitum Ludovicum de Pictavia" as his heir with "filio masculo Aimareto nepote suo nato ex eo" as substitute (and 
2 CONC naming his other sons and "Aimaretum filium domini Bermundi de Vouta et Helienos filiæ suæ" as further substitutes)[1417].  Comte de Valentinois et de Diois.  The testament of "Ludovicus de Pictavia Comes Valentinensis et Diensis"
2 CONC , dated 23 May 1345, chooses burial "in ecclesia Fratrum Minorum de Crista Diensis diocesis", donates property to the church of Viviers in memory of "Ludovicum episcopum Metensem patruum suum", appoints "filium suum unigenitum Aim
2 CONC arum de Pictavia" as his heir, with "fratrem suum Aimarum de Pictavia...Henricum...et...Karolum de Pictavia...fratres suos...avunculum suum dominum Amedeum de Pictavia et post eum Aimarum filium suum...filium primo nasciturum ex..
2 CONC .filia sua Margarita uxore domini Guichardi de Belloioco...Aimarum de Vouta nepotem suum...Ludovicus eius fratrem" in order as successive substitutes, provides for the dowry of "Margaritæ filiæ suæ uxori domini Guichardi de Belloi
2 CONC oco", and provides for "Sibiliæ de Baucio...matri suæ...consorti suæ Margaritæ de Vergy"[1418].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contracts 20 May 1319 and Paris 23 Jul 1321, Papal dispensation 1 Jul 1319) MARGUERITE de Vergy Dame de Vadans, daughter of HENRI de Vergy Seigneur de Fouvent & his wife Mathilde de Dammartin (-after Jul 1357).  The marri
2 CONC age contract of "Henricus de Vergeio dominus Fontisuennæ senescallus Burgundiæ...Mehaudis de Dampmartin...uxoris suæ...Margaritæ filiæ ipsorum" and "Aimari de Pictavia primogeniti Valentinensis comitis et Diensis" is dated 20 May 
2 CONC 1319[1419].  The testament of "Ludovicus de Pictavia Comes Valentinensis et Diensis", dated 23 May 1345, provides for "..consorti suæ Margaritæ de Vergy"[1420].  “Marguerite de Vergy comtesse de Valentinois et Marguerite de Poitie
2 CONC rs sa fille dame de Perreux” sold “le château et la seigneurie de Vadans” to the duke of Burgundy by charter dated 1357[1421].  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Comte Louis & his wife had two children: 
