1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pere_de_X%C3%A8rica
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ARAGONESE%20NOBILITY.htm#PedroEjericadied1362<br/>
2 CONT b)         PEDRO de Ejérica ([1302]-1362).  The Chronicle of Ramon Muntaner names "le noble don Jacques de Xirica…et son frère don Pedro de Xirica" among those present at the coronation of Alfonso IV King of Aragon (in 1328)[416].
2 CONC   He succeeded his brother in 1335 as Barón de Ejérica.  Zurita records the death in 1335 of “don Jayme Señor de Exerica” and the succession of “don Pedro su hermano”[417].  He supported dowager Queen Leonor, widow of Alfonso IV K
2 CONC ing of Aragon, in her struggle with her stepson Pedro IV King of Aragon over her own sons' rights, and was threatened with prosecution in 1338.  Reconciled with the King, he was appointed Governor of Valencia and became one of Ped
2 CONC ro IV's main allies in the latter's struggle with the unionist movement in Aragon led by the King's brother Jaime.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 1328, 1331) BONAVENTURA di Arborea, daughter of UGONE [II] di Basso [Serra=Cervera] Giudice di Arborea & his wife --- (-[1375/78]).  Zurita records the marriage contract agreed 1328 between “don Pedro de Exerica”
2 CONC  and “doña Buenauentura de Arborea...hija mayor del Iuez de Arborea”[418].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (1): MARÍA Pérez, daughter of ---.  Pedro & his wife had four children:
