1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL.htm#InesCastillaMGuillaumeVIIIMontpellier
2 CONT
2 CONT vi)       INÉS González de Marañón (-after Jan 1182).  A charter dated Jan 1182 records the entry of her daughter Inés in the Cistercian monastery of Aza, in the presence of her mother "Mayor García", subscribed by her children "F
2 CONC ernando, Pedro, Alberico, Nuño, Domicio, Inés"[2017].  same person as…?  INÉS (-after 4 Nov 1202).  Salazar y Castro suggests that Inés, daughter of González Rodríguez de Marañón, was the second wife of Guillaume [VII] Seigneur de
2 CONC  Montpellier[2018].  However, his hypothesis appears based only on her name and the favourable chronology.  The Thalamus de Montpellier records the marriage in May 1187 at Barcelona of "G. de Montpellier" and "sa molher Naunes"[20
2 CONC 19].  The contract of marriage between "Guillelmus Montispellusani dominus" and "Agnetem" is dated Apr 1187[2020].  "Guillelmus…Montispessulani, filius quondam Mathildis ducisse" names "domine Agnetis" as mother of his son Guillau
2 CONC me in his charter dated Dec 1197[2021].  Her family relationship with the kings of Aragon is confirmed by the charter dated 1187 under which "Ildefonsus rex Aragon, comes Barchinon. et marchio Provinciæ" granted property to "Guill
2 CONC . Montispessuli domino et uxori tuæ Agneti consanguineæ meæ"[2022].  Her precise relationship with the Aragonese kings has not yet been ascertained.  Salazar y Castro suggests that it was through her mother whose parentage is not 
2 CONC known[2023].  The marriage was declared void by the Pope in 1194[2024].  Her husband, in his testament dated 4 Nov 1202, named "Agnes uxor mea"[2025].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (Barcelona, Apr 1187) as his second (bigamous) wife, GUILLAUME [VIII] Seigneur de Montpellier, son of GUILLAUME [VII] Seigneur de Montpellier & his wife Mathilde de Bourgogne (-[Nov/Dec] 1202). 
