1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MATHILDE de Bourgogne ([1135]-before 29 Sep 1173).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to, but does not name, one of the sisters (named first in the list of sisters) of "Lingones…episcopus Galterus 
2 CONC [et] episcopum Eduensem Henricum" as "mater Guilelmi de Montepessulano domni"[270].  The contract of marriage between "Guillelmus Montispessulani dominus" and "Mathildem sororem Ducis Burgundiæ" is dated 25 Feb 1157, and names "Gu
2 CONC illelmus de Tortosa frater meus"[271].  Under his testament dated 29 Sep 1173, "Guillelmus dominus Montispessulani, filius quondam Sibilie" states that his wife Mathilde was already deceased and requests payment of her debts[272].
2 CONC   m (contract Montpellier 25 Feb 1157) GUILLAUME [VII] Seigneur de Montpellier, son of GUILLAUME [VI] Seigneur de Montpellier & his wife Sibila de Mataplana (-[29 Sep 1172/May 1173], bur Abbaye de Granselve).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDY.htm
