1 NOTE Dona Muna Elvira was the eldest sister of the Queen of Leon, and daughterof the Count of Castile.
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "EL MAYOR"
1 NOTE Muniadona Sánchez ( 995 - d.1066). También llamadada Mayor o Munia, fue condesa de Castilla (1029-1032), condesa de Ribagorza (1017-1032) y reina consorte de Pamplona.
2 CONT Tabla de contenidos
2 CONT ocultar
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 Orígenes familiares
2 CONT     * 2 Matrimonios y descendientes
2 CONT     * 3 Condado de Ribagorza
2 CONT     * 4 Condado de Castilla
2 CONT
2 CONT Orígenes familiares editar
2 CONT
2 CONT Hija de conde de Castilla Sancho García y de su mujer Urraca Gómez de la familia condal Banu Gómez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matrimonios y descendientes editar
2 CONT
2 CONT El año 1010 se casa con el futuro rey Sancho III "el Mayor" de Pamplona.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fruto de este matrimonio tuvo cuatro hijos:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Fernando Sánchez, conde de Castilla, rey de Castilla y León.
2 CONT     * García Sánchez III de Pamplona (a 1020-1054), rey de Pamplona.
2 CONT     * Gonzalo I de Ribagorza (? -1045), conde de Sobrarbe y Ribagorza.
2 CONT     * el infante Bernardo de Navarra (?-1024).
2 CONT
2 CONT Condado de Ribagorza editar
2 CONT
2 CONT En 1017 fue designada condesa Ribagorza tras la muerte sin descendencia del Conde Guillermo. Munia fue escogida por los nobles de dio condado por ser biznieta del conde Ramón II de Ribagorza y por su matrimonio con Sancho III de N
2 CONC avarra. En 1018
2 CONT  las tropas navarras invadieron la parte central del condado.
2 CONT
2 CONT Condado de Castilla editar
2 CONT
2 CONT La muerte del infante García Sánchez de Castilla (1029), asesinado por los de la familia Vela en León, permitió heredar a Sancho el Mayor el condado, por ser su esposa Muniadona hermana del difunto.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Predecesor:
2 CONT Guillermo 	Condesa de Ribagorza
2 CONT 1017 - 1032 	Sucesor:
2 CONT Gonzalo I
2 CONT Predecesor:
2 CONT García Sánchez 	Condesa de Castilla
2 CONT 1029 - 1035
2 CONT 	Sucesor:
2 CONT Fernando Sánchez
1 NOTE Mayor of Castile (died 1032) was queen of Navarre. She was originally called Muniadona (or Muñadona) and is variously called Munia (or Muña) Mayor (or just Munia or Muña). In Spanish, she is called Muniadona de Castilla. It is 
2 CONC said that her husband Sancho III of Navarre (Sancho the Great) renamed her from her contemporary name Muniadona to Mayor, for she was the eldest in her family, yet since she had an aunt of the same name, the story is clearly apocr
2 CONC yphal. She was the daughter of Count Sancho García of Castile. Her marriage to Sancho made her Queen consort of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1029, the Count García Sánchez of Castile, Mayor's brother, was assassinated by the Vela family, Castilian exiles in León. Mayor's husband, Sancho the Great, claimed his role as feudal overlord to pass the county to their se
2 CONC cond son, Ferdinand. Likewise this brought a nominal legitimate claim to the counties of Ribagorza and Sobrarbe to her husband, who has already taken control of them militarily.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mayor was the mother of four sons and perhaps two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT King García Sánchez III of Navarre 
2 CONT Ferdinand the Great, king of León and Castile 
2 CONT Gonzalo of Sobrarbe and Ribagorza 
2 CONT Bernardo 
2 CONT Jimena, wife of Bermudo III of León 
2 CONT Mayor, wife of Pons of Toulouse 
