0 @N6000000002188623978@ NOTE Eleanor of Guzman
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor of Guzman (ca 1310 – 1351) was a mistress of King Alfonso XI of Castile. She is known in Spanish as Leonor Núñez de Guzmán.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was born in Seville, daughter of the Castilian nobles Pedro Núñez de Guzmán (descendant of the noble family of Saint Dominic) and Juana Ponce de León (great-granddaughter of King Alfonso IX of León), and sister of Alfonso Núñe
1 CONC z de Guzmán (ca 1300 – Gibraltar, 1342), Master of the Order of Santiago, married ca 1330 to Dona Dona María de La Cerda, 1st Lady of Villafranca de Valcárcel (ca 1290 –), without issue.
1 CONT
1 CONT Eleanor and Alfonso had ten children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Pedro Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lord of Aguilar de Campoo (1330 - 1338).
1 CONT     * Juana Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lady of Trastamara (born 1330).
1 CONT     * Sancho Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lord of Ledesma (1331 - 1343).
1 CONT     * Enrique Alfonso of Castile, 1st Count of Trastamara (1334 - 1379), in future king Henry II of Castile.
1 CONT     * Fadrique Alfonso of Castile, Master of the Order of Santiago and 1st Lord of Haro; (born 1335).
1 CONT     * Fernando Alfonso of Castile, 2nd Lord of Ledesma.
1 CONT     * Tello Alfonso of Castile, 2nd Lord of Aguilar de Campoo (born 1337).
1 CONT     * Juan Alfonso of Castile, 1st Lord of Badajoz and Jerez de la Frontera (1341 - 1359).
1 CONT     * Sancho Alfonso of Castile, 1st Count of Alburquerque (born 1342).
1 CONT     * Pedro Alfonso of Castile (1345 - 1359).
