0 @N6000000002187820521@ NOTE Marguerite of Anjou and Maine
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Marguerite of Anjou and Maine (1273– December 31, 1299), Countess of Anjou and Maine, was the first wife of Charles of Valois a son of Philip III of France. Marguerite was a daughter of Charles II of Naples and Maria of Hungary. S
1 CONC he married Charles at Corbeil on August 16, 1290. Their children included:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Isabelle (1292-1309). Wife of John III, Duke of Brittany
1 CONT     * Philip VI of France
1 CONT     * Jeanne of Valois (1294-1342). Wife of William I, Count of Hainaut
1 CONT     * Marguerite of Valois (1295-1342). Wife of Guy I of Blois-Châtillon
1 CONT     * Charles II of Alençon (1297-1346)
1 CONT     * Catherine of Valois (1299-?)
