0 @N6000000005598851150@ NOTE Robert was sent into Burges to avenge themassacer at Burges on 18 May 1302.  His army is said to have incuded 50,000 men-at-arms including a large contingent of well armoured knights.  Facing Robert were 20,00 0 Flemish.  The two 
1 CONC armies met south of Burges on 11 July 1302.  The F lemings had chosen their ground well and awaited the French with thei r pikes on ground criss-crossed with canals.  Robert sent first a voll ey of crossbows, then a charge of knig
1 CONC hts riding over their own bowma n mired in the soft ground.  The knights advanced across the canal, mi red themselves in the adjacent marsh and heaved their way up the slop e toward the Flemish position.  Weighed down by their arm
1 CONC our and unabl e to rise from the marsh, the Flemish fell upon them.  Methodically th eir long pikes rose and fell quite remorselessly and the knights were slaughtered.  Robert was killed along with 700 of his knightly nobles of hi
1 CONC gh degree.  The battle came to be known as the 'Battle of the Spu rs'.
0 @N6000000002187845526@ NOTE Mahaut, Countess of Artois
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Mahaut of Artois (1268 – October 27, 1329, Paris), also known as Mathilda, was the daughter of Robert II, Count of Artois and Amicie de Courtenay.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married Otto IV, Count of Burgundy, to whom she bore three children, including two girls who married kings of France, Blanche and Jeanne. Because of the premature death of her brother Philip in 1298, she inherited the County o
1 CONC f Artois at her father's death in 1302, rather than her nephew Robert (her inheritance being based upon proximity of blood). Although he repeatedly challenged the decision, her rights to the County were consistently upheld. At her
1 CONC  death, the county was inherited by her daughter Jeanne II, Countess Palatine of Burgundy (d 1330), who was married to Philip V of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT She is portrayed by Jeanne Moreau in the 2005 French miniseries "Les Rois Maudits".
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Robert II Countess of Artois
1 CONT 1302–1329 Succeeded by
1 CONT Jeanne
