1 CONT
1 CONT Infanta Maria of Portugal (6 April 1342 - AFT 1363), pron. IPA: [m?'?i?], was a Portuguese infanta, first daughter of King Peter I of Portugal and his Queen consort Constance of Peñafiel.
1 CONT
1 CONT Maria was born in Évora on April 6, 1342. In 1354 she married Infante Fernando of Aragon, Marquis of Tortosa, son of Aragonese King Alfonso IV.
1 CONT
1 CONT Fernando was murdered by his half-brother Peter IV of Aragon in 1363. Maria then returned to Portugal where she died in the city of Aveiro in a year after 1363. She is buried in the Convent of Saint Claire of Coimbra.
0 @N6000000002322303415@ NOTE His reign was marked by three wars with Castile and by the growth of the
