0 @N6000000002188376402@ NOTE Blanche II of Navarre
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche II (1420-1464) was the daughter of John II of Aragon and Blanche I of Navarre.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married Henry IV of Castile. Blanca remained a virgin, not only on her wedding night, but for the rest of her marriage. After thirteen years, Henry sought the annulment of the marriage. An official examination confirmed the vi
1 CONC rginity of Blanca. A divorce was granted by the Pope on the grounds that some "witchcraft" had prevented Henry from consummating the marriage. Blanca was sent home, where her family imprisoned her, and she was later killed by pois
1 CONC on in 1464. She remained childless throughout her life.
1 CONT
1 CONT After the death of her brother in 1461, some Navarrese dissatisfied elements and some of the anti-Aragonese party regarded Blanca as the rightful monarch, as they had regarded Charles. They proclaimed her queen. She would have thu
1 CONC s become Blanche II of Navarre, had not her father (who wanted to keep the government of Navarre) already had her incarcerated and thus not capable to act. Upon her death, her rights to Navarre were inherited by her next sister, E
1 CONC leanor of Aragon, Countess of Foix, who however was their father's ally and supporter, and did not press her own claims until his death in 1479.
