0 @N6000000005598851769@ NOTE Blanche has been styled as one of the most 'beautiful ladies in the wo rld'.  She however was not a good wife for Charles and is said to hav e gone mad.  In early 1314, Philip IV had Blanche and her sister-in-la ws arrested for in
1 CONC trigues against the crown and an affair with the bro thers Philippe and Gautier D'Aunay.  She was imprisoned at Chateau de Gaillard and while in prison gave birth to a child of one of her jaile rs.  She continued to defend herself
1 CONC  agains the charges of Philip IV for seven years.  The twelve peers of France however advised Charles t o seek another wife.  After her release she was repudiated by Charles IV in 1322, then subsequently died in a convent.
0 @N6000000002187845543@ NOTE Robert, Count of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert, Count of Burgundy (1300-1315) was the son of Otto IV, Count of Burgundy and Mahaut, Countess of Artois. He was Count of Burgundy between 1302 and 1315. He died in 1315, and was succeeded by his sister, Jeanne.
