1 CONT Henry III, eldest son of King John I, at age 9  succeededhis father to the throne of England in 1216.  Henry IIIruled until 1272, and was succeeded by his eldest son,Edward I, known as Longshanks.
1 CONT  Henry III became King of England at age 9, succeeded hisfather, King John I to the throne.  Henry III was underthe Regency of William Marshall, earl of Pembroke from 1216to 1219 when Marshall died.
