1 CONT !From "Ancestral Roots of 60 Colonist" by WEIS, 6th ed, line 1, page 3; "Edward I, King ofEngland, 1272-1307, b 16 or 17 June 1239 at Westminister, d near Carlisle 7 Jul 1307; crowned 19 Aug 1274; m (1) 18 Oct 1254 Eleanor of Cast
1 CONC ile (110-30) d 1290; m (2) 8 Sep 1299 Marguerite of France (155-30). (CP V 736; CCN 353; DNB xvii, 14; xvii, 178)." 27 more generations of ancestry in this book, beyond Edward I, one goes to Alfred the Great 871-901, born Wantage 
1 CONC 849 d 26 Oct 899, the son of Aethelwulf, King of Wessex & his wife, Alswitha. She the dau of Earl Aethelred of Mercia. (Line 161, page 107). (Mercia was central England Kingdom).
0 @N6000000007329543374@ NOTE [] date of accession 1272. House of Plantagenet..  [reposted from fidonet
1 CONT by mari -at- netcom.com]: Edward I   Longshanks...  Defeated and killed
1 CONT Simon De Montfort at Eversham in 1265 and   reclaimed the  throne;
1 CONT Conquered Wales in 1284; ....
1 CONT [Collier, fidonet July '95]  EDWARD I  ENGLISH - COLLIER  Compiled by
1 CONT Leroy and Mildred (English) Collier.  GEN. 1 EDWARD,  Earl of Chester,
1 CONT third son of Henry III, King of   England,  ascended  to the throne of
1 CONT England as King Edward I. He was  born at  Westminister  on 17 June 1239.
1 CONT He ruled from 1272  to  1307.  He   married  Eleanor of Castile in 1254.
1 CONT She was a daughter of Ferdinand III, King   of  Leon, and his second
1 CONT wife, Joanna, d/o Simon de  Dammartin,  Count   d'Aumale,  and his wife,
1 CONT Marie, Countess of  Ponthiru. Joanna de Dammartin  was   a direct
1 CONT descendant of Charlemagne, being in  the 20th generation.  Edward I   and
1 CONT Eleanor had  nine  children, the  fourth child being Edward,  Prince   of
1 CONT Wales,  who  became  King Edward II.  //
0 @N6000000008630637724@ NOTE , Edward I (Longshanks), King of England
