1 CONT Berengaria was daughter of Alfonso IX, King of Leon, who was father of Ferdinand III, King of Castile and Leon and the father of Eleanor, first wife of Edward I and mother of Edward II.
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://users.adelphia.net/~hwaller/Noble.htm>
0 @N6000000003658751440@ NOTE From Plantagenet Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT BÉRENGÈRE (or BERENGUELA) OF CASTILE-LEÓN, born in 1204.  She married at Burgos in Castile in 1223 (as his 3rd wife) JEAN DE BRIENNE, Count of Brienne (as regent for his nephew), 1205-1221, King Consort of Jerusalem, 1210-1212, Ki
1 CONC ng-Regent of Jerusalem, 1212-1225, Emperor-Regent of Constantinople, son of Érard II de Brienne ... by Agnes. ... He was born 1169-74. They had three sons, Alphonse ..., Jean, and Louis, Knt. ... and one daughter, Marie. ... Jean 
1 CONC married (1st) at Tyre 14 Sept. 1210 MARIE DE MONFERRAT [[sic]], Queen of Jerusalem. ... Marie was born at Tyre in the summer of 1191.  They had one daughter, Isabel (wife of Frederick II, Holy Roman Emperor).  He was elected King 
1 CONC of Jerusalem in 1210, in right of his wife, Marie, who died soon afterwards in 1212, leaving a daughter and heiress, in whose right he subsequently reigned.  He married (2nd) in 1213 STÉPHANIE OF ARMENIA, daughter and heiress of L
1 CONC eo II, King of Armenia.  They had one son, Jean.  Stéphanie died in 1219 during the siege of Damietta.  Jean was a legatee in the 1222 will of Philippe Auguste, King of France.  In 1223 he went to France and assisted in the corona
1 CONC tion of Louis VIII, King of France, at Paris.  The same year he also visited Henry III, King of England, and received rich gifts from the king and English nobles.  In 1228 he commanded the Papal troops that ravaged Emperor Frederi
1 CONC ck's lands in southern Italy.  He was elected Latin Emperor of Constantinople in 1229, as colleague for the minor, Baldwin II.  He was crowned Emperor in the Cathedral of St. Sophia in 1231.  JEAN I (DE BRIENNE), Emperor-Regent of
1 CONC  Constantinople, died at Constantinople 21 March 1237.  His widow, Bérengère, died 12 April 1237.
