1 CONC rges of treachery.  In 1225, the c ouncil of Bourges excommunicated the count of Toulouse, Raymond VII, a nd declared a crusade against the southern barons. Louis happily renew ed the conflict in order to enforce his royal rights.
1 CONC  Roger Bernard th e Great, count of Foix, tried to keep the peace, but the king rejecte d his embassy and the counts of Foix and Toulouse took up arms agains t him. The king was largely successful, but he did not complete the wo r
1 CONC k before his death.
