0 @N6000000002188378478@ NOTE Peter V of Aragon
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Peter V of Aragon (IV of Barcelona) (1429–1466), Constable of Portugal and Grand Master of the Order of Aviz.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was son of Pedro, Duke of Coimbra and Isabella of Aragon, Countess of Urgel. Thus his paternal grandparents were King John I of Portugal and Philippa of Lancaster, and maternal ones were James II, Count of Urgel (grandson of Ja
1 CONC mes I, Count of Urgell) and Isabel of Aragon (daughter of King Peter IV of Aragon).
1 CONT
1 CONT During the War Against John II, between 1463 and 1466 Peter was King of Aragon and Count of Barcelona.
1 CONT
1 CONT Note that Peter V did not reign in Valencia, which remained under the control of John II.
