0 @N6000000002322312740@ NOTE After her marriage to John Henry, Prince of Luxembourg, she expelled John
1 CONT Henry in November 1341; whereupon Louis, declaring that the marriage had not
1 CONT been consumated and was therefore void, married her with ill-considered haste
1 CONT to his widowed son, Louis of Brandenberg, on February 10, 1342. This created
1 CONT unfavourable impression throughout the empire. A new election was held and
1 CONT Charles of Moravia, who granted excessive concessions to the Pope, was elected
1 CONT new German king, July 1346. Louis died of a heart attack in 1347 bear hunting.
