0 @N6000000002187755322@ NOTE Sancho VI of Navarre
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sancho VI Garces, (c.1133 – June 27, 1194), King of Navarre (1150-1194). He was called el Sabio ("The Wise").
1 CONT
1 CONT Son of Garcia Ramirez and Marguerite de l'Aigle, he was the first to use the name of "King of Navarre" as the only designation of his kingdom, dropping Pamplona out of the titulary use. His reign was full of clashes with Castile a
1 CONC nd Aragon.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Sancha of Castile in 1157, the daughter of Alfonso VII. Their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Sancho VII of Navarre 
1 CONT Ramiro, Bishop of Pamplona 
1 CONT Berengaria of Navarre d 1230/32 
1 CONT Blanca of Navarre, married Count Theobald III of Champagne, then acted as regent of Champagne, and finally as regent of Navarre. 
1 CONT He died on June 27, 1194 in Pamplona.
1 CONT
1 CONT   This biography of a European noble is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Garcia VI King of Navarre
1 CONT 1150–1194 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Sancho VII 
